WEBVTT

00:25.342 --> 00:45.010
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:51.342 --> 00:53.010
I swear to God, I didn't touch shit!

00:53.011 --> 00:55.763
So the gate just opened up all on its own,
like magic?

00:55.764 --> 00:57.806
It must've been some kind of malfunction.

00:57.807 --> 00:59.183
Let me get this straight.

00:59.184 --> 01:02.770
There was a malfunction
at the exact moment that truck showed up?

01:02.771 --> 01:04.563
You expect me to believe that, soldier?

01:04.564 --> 01:06.315
I swear. I don't know what happened.

01:06.316 --> 01:08.651
What if it <i>was</i> a malfunction?

01:09.569 --> 01:12.697
Only one not caused by us.

01:28.713 --> 01:30.839
All right, lab rats, let's scurry up.

01:30.840 --> 01:34.636
An entire dimension's about
to come crashing down on our heads.

01:37.305 --> 01:38.431
Hey.

01:39.557 --> 01:40.683
Is everything okay?

01:41.851 --> 01:42.768
Listen,

01:42.769 --> 01:46.105
I know this plan is totally mad,
and a million things have to go right,

01:46.106 --> 01:48.941
and a million things could
and probably will go wrong.

01:48.942 --> 01:52.112
But we can do this. I know it.

01:52.695 --> 01:56.074
One last fight,
and this whole nightmare, it'll be over.

01:56.658 --> 01:58.243
It'll finally be over.

02:31.651 --> 02:33.402
Well, hello there.

02:33.403 --> 02:35.612
MAC, this is Wolfpack. Do you copy--

02:35.613 --> 02:37.990
- What do you think you're doing?
- Alerting the Doc.

02:37.991 --> 02:39.992
That bitch has a God complex.

02:39.993 --> 02:41.870
All she'll do is slow us down.

02:42.453 --> 02:43.288
No.

02:43.913 --> 02:45.999
We're bagging this freak ourselves.

04:53.501 --> 04:56.545
- Do you think they're all right?
- The truck is faster than a Humvee.

04:56.546 --> 04:59.256
Let's be conservative,
say five miles faster.

04:59.257 --> 05:01.800
They had a six minute,
20 second head start,

05:01.801 --> 05:04.386
giving them an additional lead
of about half a mile.

05:04.387 --> 05:06.805
So they're fine for now,

05:06.806 --> 05:09.766
but the real shit hasn't started yet.

05:09.767 --> 05:11.685
Erica, language, please.

05:11.686 --> 05:15.940
This isn't Intro to Science.
This situation demands cussing.

05:19.694 --> 05:22.946
- So, how's it feel?
- What?

05:22.947 --> 05:26.451
Helping to save the world and all that.

05:27.327 --> 05:28.995
It feels pretty swell.

05:29.787 --> 05:31.748
Pretty goddamn swell.

05:44.469 --> 05:45.844
Go! Go! Go!

05:45.845 --> 05:48.222
Breach! Move, move, move!

06:16.793 --> 06:18.335
Hey, Robin, yeah.

06:18.336 --> 06:20.420
Can you please tell me that
that was you guys

06:20.421 --> 06:22.590
and not more of those, like, mutant Cujos?

06:23.383 --> 06:26.051
It's us, and it's too early
to be stressed, Vic. Save it for later.

06:26.052 --> 06:29.722
Yeah, no, copy that, yeah. No.
Bottling... Bottling emotions.

06:35.728 --> 06:39.565
No sign of an evil moving planet.

06:40.316 --> 06:43.111
Well, that's good.
'Cause this is gonna take some time.

06:43.694 --> 06:45.196
All right, we should split up.

06:45.822 --> 06:47.240
Use both ladders.

06:47.740 --> 06:49.950
Don't rush. Pace yourselves.

06:49.951 --> 06:53.829
There are platforms along the way,
so use them to rest.

06:53.830 --> 06:54.914
All right.

06:56.582 --> 06:57.875
Let's do this.

07:43.129 --> 07:44.130
You okay?

07:54.015 --> 07:55.682
Don't be frightened.

07:55.683 --> 07:57.268
These are all friends.

07:57.977 --> 07:59.562
They're just here to watch.

08:00.146 --> 08:01.814
Don't focus on them.

08:02.398 --> 08:03.858
<i>Yes, Papa.</i>

08:16.704 --> 08:20.958
And let there be light.

08:25.004 --> 08:27.672
All right, nice work, Bald Eagle.

08:27.673 --> 08:29.341
Now get up to the roof.

08:29.342 --> 08:31.302
Careful with that C-4.

08:31.886 --> 08:33.763
I don't wanna blow the Upside Down
with us in it.

08:34.514 --> 08:36.681
Oh, I was planning on carelessness.

08:36.682 --> 08:39.602
But you're right, Jim.
Caution here would be wise.

08:46.400 --> 08:47.276
All right.

08:48.569 --> 08:50.028
Now remember,

08:50.029 --> 08:53.908
two slow knocks means...

08:54.408 --> 08:57.327
- The Abyss started to move.
- That's right.

08:57.328 --> 09:01.331
And you and your sister get in position,
but you wait. You do not attack.

09:01.332 --> 09:04.459
The second I get confirmation
that planet's close enough to the tower,

09:04.460 --> 09:07.462
then I'm gonna give you three fast knocks.

09:07.463 --> 09:09.714
Then we strike. We kill Henry.

09:09.715 --> 09:15.513
And we, uh, pray to God Dustin's right,
and that planet stops moving.

09:16.722 --> 09:19.141
What could possibly go wrong, right?

09:21.227 --> 09:23.396
If something does go wrong,

09:24.188 --> 09:26.816
I need you to promise me
you won't pull me out.

09:27.817 --> 09:29.694
Not until I'm sure he's dead.

09:33.364 --> 09:34.282
Okay, well,

09:35.491 --> 09:37.742
then I'm gonna need a promise
from you too.

09:37.743 --> 09:41.079
If by some miracle this plan works,
we're getting the hell out of here.

09:41.080 --> 09:45.585
Doc Kay and her plans,
that's a problem for another day.

09:47.378 --> 09:48.421
Deal?

10:02.476 --> 10:03.978
Let's end this, kid.

11:16.425 --> 11:18.094
- You want some?
- Yeah.

11:30.022 --> 11:31.774
Hey, um...

11:32.775 --> 11:35.403
What you said earlier at the Squawk...

11:36.696 --> 11:37.780
I'm sorry.

11:38.489 --> 11:41.533
I mean, not sorry about what you said.
That came out wrong.

11:41.534 --> 11:43.743
Or not came out wrong. Jesus Christ.

11:43.744 --> 11:44.995
It's okay.

11:45.871 --> 11:47.372
No, it's... it's not.

11:47.373 --> 11:50.792
I should have been there for you,
and I wasn't.

11:50.793 --> 11:54.754
And I guess I was just so self-absorbed
that I couldn't see it.

11:54.755 --> 11:57.550
I just... I feel like an idiot, and I...

11:58.759 --> 11:59.635
I'm sorry.

12:00.219 --> 12:04.055
You don't have to be sorry.
And you are not an idiot. You're not.

12:04.056 --> 12:05.266
It's just...

12:06.350 --> 12:10.396
I didn't even understand it myself
for the longest time.

12:11.939 --> 12:15.066
I just... I think it needed to happen
the way it happened.

12:15.067 --> 12:16.610
I needed to find my own way.

12:17.319 --> 12:19.904
But what matters is
that you're still here,

12:19.905 --> 12:22.491
and you still think we can be friends.

12:23.075 --> 12:24.827
Friends? No, thanks.

12:26.120 --> 12:27.288
Best friends.

12:29.874 --> 12:31.375
All right, come on.

12:33.502 --> 12:34.670
We've got a planet to catch.

12:37.506 --> 12:39.382
<i>What the hell is taking them so long?</i>

12:39.383 --> 12:43.262
I don't know. Maybe it has something to do
with the fact that it's a 500-foot tower.

12:44.013 --> 12:45.847
If something's wrong, they'll contact us.

12:45.848 --> 12:48.559
Yeah, no, yeah.
I mean, unless they're already dead.

12:50.394 --> 12:53.647
Okay, uh, stress gives me
the munchies, so I, um...

12:55.149 --> 12:56.399
Do you want anything?

12:56.400 --> 12:57.525
No.

12:57.526 --> 12:58.569
Okay.

12:59.820 --> 13:00.863
Actually, can I get a--

13:03.240 --> 13:04.241
Vickie?

13:06.035 --> 13:07.077
Vickie!

13:34.021 --> 13:35.189
Holy shit.

14:01.966 --> 14:05.678
Mm. I swear to God,
nothing cures anxiety quite like a bowl--

14:37.293 --> 14:38.627
Trippy, isn't it?

14:42.298 --> 14:43.173
Hi.

14:57.897 --> 14:59.023
Thanks, man.

14:59.565 --> 15:00.733
Okay.

15:11.702 --> 15:13.495
It's pretty damn spectacular.

15:15.080 --> 15:17.166
It's almost too bad
we have to blow it all up.

15:30.679 --> 15:32.389
Mother of God.

15:49.990 --> 15:52.575
Jim, do you, uh, copy?

15:52.576 --> 15:54.118
Yeah, yeah, copy.

15:54.119 --> 15:56.412
<i>Well, I got some good news, bad news.</i>

15:56.413 --> 15:58.498
<i>Uh, good news is our theory was correct.</i>

15:58.499 --> 16:01.250
<i>A giant planet is descending
upon our heads.</i>

16:01.251 --> 16:04.045
The bad news is our theory was correct.

16:04.046 --> 16:07.131
A giant planet is descending
upon our heads.

16:07.132 --> 16:09.258
- How long do we have?
<i>- Not long.</i>

16:09.259 --> 16:11.553
Supergirl better be close in there.

16:17.643 --> 16:18.978
Come on, El.

16:35.244 --> 16:38.414
So this is Vecna, right now in the Abyss?

16:39.456 --> 16:41.792
You don't have to whisper, but yes.

16:42.459 --> 16:45.795
Okay, so why don't we just kill him
right here?

16:45.796 --> 16:47.630
I mean, he seems pretty damn vulnerable.

16:47.631 --> 16:48.798
We can't hurt him here.

16:48.799 --> 16:50.258
We have to enter his mind.

16:50.259 --> 16:51.759
- Isn't this his mind?
- No.

16:51.760 --> 16:53.261
- It's my mind.
- What?

16:53.262 --> 16:54.221
Hold on.

17:07.192 --> 17:08.318
Are you okay?

17:11.155 --> 17:12.448
Oh, great.

17:13.032 --> 17:15.075
I've really missed this.

17:15.826 --> 17:16.702
Hop.

17:18.662 --> 17:20.079
The Abyss is moving.

17:20.080 --> 17:22.498
- How close are we to Henry's house?
- Not close.

17:22.499 --> 17:24.542
- How not close?
- I'm not sure.

17:24.543 --> 17:26.419
You said you know his mind
backwards and forwards.

17:26.420 --> 17:29.422
Yeah, I do, but there are a shit ton
of memories in here.

17:29.423 --> 17:32.633
We're like Dorothy in Oz,
except there's no Yellow Brick Road.

17:32.634 --> 17:35.470
Everything connects,
but there are long ways and short ways.

17:35.471 --> 17:37.764
- Well, we need a short way.
- Yeah, no shit.

17:37.765 --> 17:40.266
Now can you just stop talking
while I try and think?

17:40.267 --> 17:43.686
- Joyce, this that stupid play of yours?
- Better see you there, Harrington.

17:43.687 --> 17:46.105
Yeah, on a Friday night? You wish.

17:46.106 --> 17:47.940
Come on, I have an idea.

17:47.941 --> 17:49.609
- Is that Joyce?
- Yep.

17:49.610 --> 17:51.819
And through that door,
Hop's sneaking a joint.

17:51.820 --> 17:54.781
And that way, Mr. Wheeler
is feeling up Mrs. Wheeler.

17:54.782 --> 17:57.826
I wish we had time to sightsee,
but we've got a play to catch.

18:14.343 --> 18:16.220
<i>Three, two, one, go!</i>

18:17.471 --> 18:19.306
<i>Yeah, we're gonna sweep around the back.</i>

18:25.104 --> 18:26.313
West room's clear.

18:33.362 --> 18:34.905
South side!

18:39.409 --> 18:42.329
<i>We are at location. Negative on...</i>

19:06.937 --> 19:09.480
No, no, no, guys. It's not lining up.

19:09.481 --> 19:10.940
What do you mean?

19:10.941 --> 19:13.527
Look. The tower needle,
it's not lining up with the rift.

19:14.361 --> 19:15.403
Shit.

19:15.404 --> 19:17.531
- If the Abyss hits the needle...
- This tower's going down.

19:18.157 --> 19:20.284
That's great. That's just great.

19:20.951 --> 19:23.411
Hey, Chief,
we're gonna need El to stop this planet.

19:23.412 --> 19:26.373
<i>- On the sooner side, please.</i>
- How soon?

19:26.957 --> 19:28.000
Thirty seconds?

19:53.150 --> 19:54.817
What are we doing?

19:54.818 --> 19:56.361
- Waiting.
- For what?

19:58.780 --> 20:00.782
Three. We need to strike.

20:03.869 --> 20:06.078
Chief, talk to me.
What's going on in there?

20:06.079 --> 20:08.664
I don't know. I can't talk to her.
I gave her the signal.

20:08.665 --> 20:10.416
Well, nothing's happening over here,

20:10.417 --> 20:14.087
and we're about to be squashed
by a moving planet. So give it again!

20:15.589 --> 20:18.342
- We have to go.
- This is the only way. Just trust me.

20:29.144 --> 20:30.229
Shit!

20:54.795 --> 20:56.171
Look out! Look out! Look out!

20:58.465 --> 20:59.967
Now!

21:11.895 --> 21:12.896
Steve!

21:18.110 --> 21:19.987
Steve!

21:38.547 --> 21:42.009
Just hold on! I got you. Just hold on!

21:52.227 --> 21:54.437
We're alive! We're alive!

21:54.438 --> 21:56.440
Shit, I thought you were toast.

21:58.567 --> 22:03.822
The Abyss stopped! El got him!
I repeat, El got the bastard!

22:04.406 --> 22:06.825
<i>Yes! Wow! Come on!</i>

22:09.786 --> 22:13.080
You came back. You came back for me.

22:13.081 --> 22:16.500
And I'm not leaving your side, ever again.

22:16.501 --> 22:18.878
Not until we're out of here. All of us.

22:18.879 --> 22:20.254
It's her! It's the monster!

22:20.255 --> 22:23.007
- Get up!
- No, I'm not the monster.

22:23.008 --> 22:24.051
And I can prove it.

22:54.498 --> 22:55.373
All clear!

22:55.374 --> 22:56.333
Hold this.

22:57.542 --> 22:58.626
- Hey!
- Easy!

22:58.627 --> 22:59.877
- You ready?
- Ready?

22:59.878 --> 23:00.837
Yeah.

23:01.630 --> 23:04.465
Okay, easy. Easy. I got you, man.

23:04.466 --> 23:06.218
All right, here goes nothing.

23:26.154 --> 23:27.823
Holy shit.

23:28.657 --> 23:30.866
Does this officially make us
space travelers?

23:30.867 --> 23:33.370
Interdimensional space travelers.

23:34.079 --> 23:36.164
Suck it, Armstrong.

24:00.814 --> 24:02.232
It's over.

24:06.111 --> 24:07.403
Where are they?

24:07.404 --> 24:09.281
With Max.

24:10.073 --> 24:11.116
Safe.

24:14.995 --> 24:16.872
Where are they?

24:17.456 --> 24:18.457
I told you.

24:19.082 --> 24:20.292
With Max.

24:21.209 --> 24:23.128
Far away from here.

24:24.713 --> 24:26.506
You can't believe it, can you?

24:27.632 --> 24:30.135
That they would ever
see through your lies.

24:32.179 --> 24:33.429
Why can't he see us?

24:33.430 --> 24:36.808
Because Mr. Whatsit isn't the only one
with magic powers.

24:42.147 --> 24:43.857
That's why you take children.

24:44.608 --> 24:48.945
Because you think they have weak minds.

24:53.408 --> 24:56.161
But they're smarter than you think.

24:57.496 --> 24:58.538
And you?

24:59.539 --> 25:01.166
Are you smart?

25:02.501 --> 25:04.586
You let yourself get caught.

25:07.506 --> 25:09.257
And in here...

25:11.051 --> 25:15.597
I will find all the answers I need.

25:31.446 --> 25:33.072
Holy shit.

25:33.073 --> 25:35.617
It's him. He's the Black Thing.

25:36.201 --> 25:40.287
Everything Holly told you is true.
He is trying to destroy our world.

25:40.288 --> 25:42.957
But he can't do it, not without you.

25:42.958 --> 25:45.919
We have to escape. Right now.

25:53.176 --> 25:54.970
Stronger, aren't we?

25:57.556 --> 25:58.848
So am I.

26:00.225 --> 26:01.101
Holly!

26:04.563 --> 26:06.147
<i>I can follow her into his mind.</i>

26:07.107 --> 26:10.110
We can end our brother, together.

26:22.789 --> 26:23.999
Come on!

26:28.461 --> 26:29.754
Now!

26:30.880 --> 26:31.965
Hello, brother.

26:55.822 --> 26:57.365
Don't know about you guys,

26:58.158 --> 27:00.451
but I was expecting more like...

27:00.452 --> 27:02.703
- Deadly vines?
- Or monsters?

27:02.704 --> 27:05.706
I assume the hive mind works here too.
So if Henry died,

27:05.707 --> 27:08.125
- so did all his nasty, little minions.
- "If"?

27:08.126 --> 27:10.794
We don't know what's going on in the mind.

27:10.795 --> 27:12.963
I know El broke the spell
and stopped the Abyss,

27:12.964 --> 27:15.008
but she could still be fighting him.

27:16.760 --> 27:19.219
Hey. She's been training for this.

27:19.220 --> 27:22.681
And she's not alone.
She's got Kali and Max.

27:22.682 --> 27:26.227
And I'm sure Henry's dead.
And if he's not, he will be.

27:27.604 --> 27:28.605
Yeah.

27:30.440 --> 27:32.150
Great job keeping the morale up.

27:35.070 --> 27:36.071
Hey, man.

27:37.697 --> 27:38.657
Hey.

27:40.700 --> 27:42.661
Thought I was a goner back there.

27:44.663 --> 27:45.914
Owe you one.

27:46.623 --> 27:47.749
Yeah.

27:50.960 --> 27:53.088
Look, just because I don't like you,

27:53.963 --> 27:55.674
doesn't mean I want you dead.

27:57.342 --> 28:00.053
And I've got a feeling
we're gonna need you up here.

28:02.138 --> 28:04.432
I don't blame you, by the way.

28:05.141 --> 28:06.850
For not liking me.

28:06.851 --> 28:10.438
You know, I can be a real prick sometimes.

28:12.273 --> 28:13.274
Yeah.

28:13.942 --> 28:16.069
I mean, same.

28:19.614 --> 28:21.116
Look, Steve,

28:22.534 --> 28:24.327
when I was away in California,

28:25.870 --> 28:28.873
you were there for Nancy
when I couldn't be.

28:30.709 --> 28:35.714
And I thought that, you know,
that was why things were off with us.

28:37.549 --> 28:38.883
But the truth is

28:39.926 --> 28:42.053
our problems had nothing to do with you.

28:43.722 --> 28:46.391
It just took me a long time
to figure that out.

28:49.352 --> 28:50.353
And...

28:51.229 --> 28:52.522
to let her go.

28:57.152 --> 28:58.819
If we hadn't been so busy fighting,

28:58.820 --> 29:02.449
I probably could've saved you
a little bit of time, because...

29:03.450 --> 29:08.079
I've known for a while now me and Nance
were never really in the cards.

29:09.289 --> 29:12.207
You know, she's independent.
She's gotta get out there, and...

29:12.208 --> 29:14.753
- I don't know. I want...
- Six little nuggets?

29:17.005 --> 29:18.089
She told you that?

29:21.384 --> 29:23.178
You think it would've been better
if I'd said four?

29:24.304 --> 29:26.889
Maybe just not calling them nuggets.

29:26.890 --> 29:27.974
Right.

29:28.933 --> 29:31.311
Listen, bottom line, end of the day, I...

29:32.103 --> 29:34.689
I'd rather have her as a friend
than nothing at all.

29:35.648 --> 29:37.900
You know, she's... she's just really...

29:37.901 --> 29:39.194
- Special.
- Yeah.

29:41.654 --> 29:43.364
I guess we can agree on one thing.

29:44.532 --> 29:46.034
Yeah, I guess so.

29:49.913 --> 29:53.291
- I still don't like you, though.
- I wouldn't want it any other way.

29:55.585 --> 29:56.794
Hey, lovebirds!

29:56.795 --> 29:58.463
You're gonna wanna check this out.

30:01.049 --> 30:03.259
Jesus Christ.

30:12.977 --> 30:13.978
That's it.

30:14.646 --> 30:16.523
That's what I saw in my vision.

30:17.649 --> 30:18.983
The kids are in there.

30:20.944 --> 30:22.612
Then what are we waiting for?

30:32.455 --> 30:34.998
Derek? No! Derek, you have to keep going.

30:34.999 --> 30:37.334
- I can't.
- Derek, what are you doing? Come on!

30:37.335 --> 30:40.379
Just leave me!
Save yourselves, you dumbasses!

30:40.380 --> 30:41.505
No, don't be an idiot!

30:41.506 --> 30:44.425
- I'm not being an idiot!
- Yes, you are! No, you can't--

30:52.600 --> 30:54.518
- Is everyone okay?
- Yeah, we're okay.

30:54.519 --> 30:57.021
- Did you find him? Tell me you found him.
- He just vanished.

30:57.814 --> 30:59.273
He went back to the real world.

30:59.274 --> 31:01.400
He can come back. <i>Will</i> come back.

31:01.401 --> 31:02.734
How far to the cave?

31:02.735 --> 31:04.279
It's not far. Come on.

31:04.863 --> 31:06.488
Derek, we gotta go. Right now.

31:06.489 --> 31:07.699
Go! Run!

31:12.954 --> 31:16.791
Dustin! Lucas!
What's going on? Come on, talk to me!

32:20.688 --> 32:22.899
You knew this would happen.

32:24.734 --> 32:28.529
Just like you know
what will happen to her.

32:30.156 --> 32:31.866
Don't you see, Jane?

32:32.492 --> 32:37.371
It's a cycle.
It's a terrible, vicious cycle.

32:37.372 --> 32:40.291
But we can stop it. Tonight.

32:44.295 --> 32:45.463
How?

32:46.047 --> 32:49.800
After we kill our brother,
after the children are rescued,

32:49.801 --> 32:53.804
we don't leave with the others.
We stay on the bridge.

32:53.805 --> 32:56.015
When the Upside Down vanishes...

32:59.102 --> 33:00.061
so will we.

33:02.647 --> 33:04.148
It is the only way, Jane.

33:05.274 --> 33:07.276
The only way.

33:08.528 --> 33:13.156
<i>She's going to do it, Jim.
She's going to end her life.</i>

33:13.157 --> 33:14.742
Show yourself!

33:15.785 --> 33:18.245
Show yourself, you lying bastard!

33:18.246 --> 33:23.709
<i>I am many things, but I am not a liar.</i>

33:23.710 --> 33:26.503
<i>I have seen into her mind,</i>

33:26.504 --> 33:29.965
<i>and now I have seen into yours.</i>

33:29.966 --> 33:32.218
<i>What rage it holds!</i>

33:32.802 --> 33:37.347
<i>One daughter dead because of you,
and soon another.</i>

33:37.348 --> 33:38.724
Show yourself!

33:38.725 --> 33:42.936
<i>You are as you fear.</i>

33:42.937 --> 33:45.732
You are the curse.

34:04.292 --> 34:05.293
No!

34:21.726 --> 34:22.935
Why's he signaling?

34:27.273 --> 34:29.525
- That's not a signal.
- Then what is it?

34:39.660 --> 34:40.620
Oh, God.

34:41.913 --> 34:43.122
Holly!

34:43.748 --> 34:45.124
Get to the cave!

34:48.252 --> 34:50.421
I got you. Hang on.

34:51.005 --> 34:51.964
Hang on!

34:54.425 --> 34:56.511
Hold on. Hold on.

35:03.309 --> 35:04.811
What did you do?

35:13.778 --> 35:14.904
Hi there.

35:29.335 --> 35:30.253
Hey, Doc.

35:30.962 --> 35:32.755
Kids left out their homework.

35:43.933 --> 35:45.725
- Max!
- What happened?

35:45.726 --> 35:48.270
She just poofed away like a goddamn ghost!

35:48.271 --> 35:50.939
Was it the Black Thing?
Did the Black Thing take them?

35:50.940 --> 35:52.232
Listen up!

35:52.233 --> 35:56.987
We keep to the plan. Get to the cave.
The Black Thing can't hurt us there.

35:56.988 --> 36:00.824
So follow me, keep quiet, and stay close.

36:00.825 --> 36:02.784
- Let's go! Come on.
- Come on, guys.

36:02.785 --> 36:04.412
Let's go! Hurry!

36:04.996 --> 36:07.998
The kids are all alone in there.
You have to get us back to them.

36:07.999 --> 36:12.002
I can't, not without the bath.
He locked us out.

36:12.003 --> 36:15.463
We have to get to the Abyss,
join the others. We can kill him there.

36:15.464 --> 36:19.259
There is no time. The worlds will collide
long before we reach him.

36:19.260 --> 36:22.012
Not if Holly and the kids make it
to the cave.

36:22.013 --> 36:26.183
If Dustin is right,
without the kids, Henry can't do anything.

36:26.184 --> 36:27.852
That's a lot of ifs.

36:28.561 --> 36:29.604
What do you wanna do?

36:31.439 --> 36:32.981
We can't give up, not now.

36:32.982 --> 36:35.651
Isn't that exactly what you're doing?
Giving up.

36:37.820 --> 36:39.322
I know the truth.

36:41.073 --> 36:42.616
Henry showed me your plan.

36:42.617 --> 36:44.284
Henry lied to you.

36:44.285 --> 36:45.827
He tricked you.

36:45.828 --> 36:48.580
He used you, and you fell for it.

36:48.581 --> 36:50.333
Then look me in the eye and tell me.

36:51.375 --> 36:52.792
Tell me.

36:52.793 --> 36:55.338
Tell me you don't plan
on killing yourself tonight.

36:57.048 --> 36:59.049
We don't have time for this.
We have to go.

36:59.050 --> 37:00.927
I won't detonate it.

37:03.179 --> 37:05.138
- I won't.
- What?

37:05.139 --> 37:06.932
I will not detonate the C-4,

37:06.933 --> 37:11.061
not until I know that you are safe
with the others back in Hawkins.

37:11.062 --> 37:16.191
If we kill Henry and don't destroy
the Upside Down, nothing matters.

37:16.192 --> 37:21.279
Which is why I will destroy it
once I know that you're safe.

37:21.280 --> 37:22.614
Why are you doing this?

37:22.615 --> 37:25.242
Because Henry's gotten to him,
and he's lost his mind.

37:25.243 --> 37:28.120
- Kali, wait.
- No. This is bigger than him, Jane.

37:28.829 --> 37:32.165
- Bigger than any of us.
- Yeah, go ahead. Go ahead. Shoot me.

37:32.166 --> 37:35.336
If I'm alive, then so is Henry.

37:36.045 --> 37:37.754
I have to end the cycle.

37:37.755 --> 37:40.757
You will. You will. But not like this.

37:40.758 --> 37:43.844
Not with more violence.
Not with more pain.

37:45.054 --> 37:47.306
There's already been so much pain.

37:47.890 --> 37:49.475
From the moment you were born.

37:49.976 --> 37:53.687
Your mother was taken from you.
Your childhood was taken from you.

37:53.688 --> 37:58.276
You've been attacked, manipulated, abused

37:59.568 --> 38:01.069
by terrible people.

38:01.070 --> 38:04.323
Life has been so unfair to you,

38:05.116 --> 38:06.284
so cruel.

38:08.119 --> 38:09.536
But you never let it break you.

38:09.537 --> 38:11.580
And I need you to fight, kid.

38:12.581 --> 38:15.167
I just need you to fight one last time.

38:16.002 --> 38:18.628
Fight for the happy days
on the other side of this.

38:18.629 --> 38:20.006
Fight for...

38:21.549 --> 38:24.385
for a world beyond Hawkins.

38:25.094 --> 38:27.722
Fight for that day
that you have a kid of your own,

38:28.889 --> 38:31.642
and you give her the life
that you never had.

38:35.146 --> 38:37.814
For the day you get so angry
because she invites some boy over,

38:37.815 --> 38:39.900
and she won't keep the door open
three inches.

38:41.527 --> 38:42.777
I know.

38:42.778 --> 38:45.364
I know you don't believe
you can have any of this.

38:45.865 --> 38:47.325
But I promise you

38:48.034 --> 38:50.244
we will find a way to make it real.

38:50.911 --> 38:53.914
<i>You</i> will find a way to make it real.

38:55.249 --> 38:56.584
Because you have to.

38:59.503 --> 39:01.130
Because you deserve it.

39:05.801 --> 39:06.634
<i>Jim!</i>

39:06.635 --> 39:08.303
<i>Jim! Are you there, Jim?</i>

39:08.304 --> 39:12.725
I don't want to add to the stress,
but we've got company.

39:33.621 --> 39:36.247
Come on! Come on!
We're almost there! Keep going!

39:36.248 --> 39:39.292
Through this gap right here! Right here!
Come on! One by one!

39:39.293 --> 39:40.586
Go! Go! Go!

39:42.671 --> 39:43.589
Debbie, wait!

39:46.634 --> 39:47.676
Have you seen Derek?

39:49.720 --> 39:51.513
- Derek!
- Wait! Holly!

39:51.514 --> 39:53.432
- Derek!
- Holly!

40:01.816 --> 40:04.901
Come on! Come on! We got this!
We gotta go! Come on! Hurry up!

40:04.902 --> 40:08.905
Keep running! Come on, Derek! Come on!

40:08.906 --> 40:11.783
Get inside. He's coming! Go!

40:11.784 --> 40:12.868
Come on!

40:17.748 --> 40:18.833
Holly!

40:26.715 --> 40:27.633
Go!

40:29.927 --> 40:31.929
- Suck my fat one!
- Come on!

40:36.392 --> 40:37.476
Holly!

40:39.145 --> 40:41.104
- Are you okay?
- We're okay. We're okay.

40:41.105 --> 40:42.480
Was it him? Was it Henry?

40:42.481 --> 40:47.694
Yes, but he can't get us. Okay?
Not in here. We're safe now.

40:47.695 --> 40:49.321
- Okay.
- We're safe.

41:12.887 --> 41:15.055
- Why are you staring at me?
- I'm not!

41:18.225 --> 41:21.519
We're just getting really close, okay?
And we don't know what's in there,

41:21.520 --> 41:24.314
so I think you should be sharing
some of that firepower.

41:24.315 --> 41:25.732
You have firepower.

41:25.733 --> 41:27.567
Three Molotovs? Come on!

41:27.568 --> 41:29.652
Unless you're okay living
with the guilt of my death,

41:29.653 --> 41:31.572
I'm gonna need one of those goddamn guns!

41:39.788 --> 41:40.831
Holy shit!

41:41.457 --> 41:42.458
Thanks!

41:45.127 --> 41:46.419
Those are flares.

41:46.420 --> 41:47.505
What?

41:48.547 --> 41:51.217
Flares. She gave you a flare gun, dude.

41:52.718 --> 41:53.843
What?

41:53.844 --> 41:55.053
Flare gun?

41:55.054 --> 41:58.557
Nancy! Nancy, what the hell is this?
Are you serious?

41:59.600 --> 42:00.976
You think this is a joke?

42:02.728 --> 42:04.563
What the hell am I gonna do
with a flare gun?

42:08.359 --> 42:10.110
<i>Hey! Will!</i>

42:11.570 --> 42:12.487
- Will!
- Will!

42:12.488 --> 42:15.365
Hey! What is it? What's wrong?

42:15.366 --> 42:16.450
It's Henry.

42:17.910 --> 42:18.786
He's alive.

42:51.610 --> 42:53.195
<i>Resist it.</i>

42:55.531 --> 42:57.366
<i>How did you find me?</i>

43:04.540 --> 43:06.000
<i>They sent you.</i>

43:08.002 --> 43:09.420
<i>Resist it.</i>

43:17.553 --> 43:19.221
Will!

43:22.141 --> 43:23.142
What was that?

43:23.726 --> 43:24.727
Holly?

43:26.437 --> 43:27.354
Stay here.

43:47.374 --> 43:49.460
What's going on? What do you see?

43:50.210 --> 43:53.630
It's Henry. He's made it into the cave.

43:53.631 --> 43:59.094
He's coming! Go! Go! Up here! Everyone!
Come on! Go, go, go, go, go!

44:00.346 --> 44:04.098
Hurry! Come on, quickly! Go! Go!

44:04.099 --> 44:07.935
He's found them.
He's found Holly and the kids.

44:07.936 --> 44:09.270
Okay, what about El?

44:09.271 --> 44:12.482
Do you see El? Or Kali? Or Max?

44:12.483 --> 44:15.277
They're alone. They're all alone.

44:17.655 --> 44:19.865
- Go! Go! Hurry!
- Come on, guys!

44:27.414 --> 44:30.458
Could you stop him? With your powers?

44:30.459 --> 44:33.128
I can try. Just keep going.

44:33.712 --> 44:34.838
Go! Go!

44:46.225 --> 44:47.810
Move! Move! Move!

45:00.781 --> 45:01.824
Come on! Come on!

45:23.929 --> 45:25.097
Oh, God.

45:40.237 --> 45:41.779
Hurry! Let's go!

45:41.780 --> 45:44.615
Quickly! Come on!
It's right up here, this hole!

45:44.616 --> 45:48.787
Joshua, down there! Be careful, okay?
Keep moving! Thomas, you next!

46:00.799 --> 46:02.301
<i>Jim, do you copy?</i>

46:02.801 --> 46:04.803
Jim, do you copy?

46:05.471 --> 46:06.764
Goddammit!

46:23.322 --> 46:24.156
Kali.

46:31.455 --> 46:35.459
Well, well. Look what we got here.

46:36.627 --> 46:38.711
Your friends just left you here, huh?

46:38.712 --> 46:40.547
Well, that's not very nice, now is it?

46:44.384 --> 46:45.344
Hmm.

46:46.136 --> 46:47.596
Get her out of here.

47:01.276 --> 47:02.444
Hey. Hey.

47:03.028 --> 47:05.280
I got you. I got you.

47:06.156 --> 47:07.908
And I got you.

47:13.664 --> 47:16.666
All right, listen.
Anything you see in here is not real.

47:16.667 --> 47:19.377
It can't hurt you.
Just keep your eyes on me, okay?

47:19.378 --> 47:20.337
- Okay.
- Okay.

47:23.674 --> 47:24.550
Come on, let's go.

47:26.927 --> 47:28.219
Keep going. Stay close.

47:28.220 --> 47:30.346
Eyes on me, okay? Eyes on me.

47:30.347 --> 47:31.682
Just keep moving.

47:33.100 --> 47:34.433
Holy shitballs!

47:34.434 --> 47:36.436
Eyes on me, Derek!

47:39.064 --> 47:42.066
Through here. You get to the other side,
and you wait for me.

47:42.067 --> 47:43.694
Debbie, you first.

47:48.115 --> 47:49.365
Thomas, your turn.

47:49.366 --> 47:51.409
- Come on, guys. Let's hurry up!
- Let's go!

47:51.410 --> 47:54.329
- Come on! Come on! We got this.
- Hurry up, Glenn.

47:57.291 --> 47:58.292
Go!

48:04.423 --> 48:08.634
Tell me where the other freak is,
or this one dies right here, right now.

48:08.635 --> 48:11.680
I don't know what you're talking about.
It's just us.

48:12.931 --> 48:15.893
You think I'm playing a game here?
Where is she?

48:28.196 --> 48:32.284
Okay. Oh, what are you doing, Murray?
This is not a good plan.

48:33.452 --> 48:34.744
This is crazy.

48:34.745 --> 48:38.832
Okay. Here goes absolutely nothing.

48:40.250 --> 48:41.835
One last chance.

48:42.628 --> 48:44.338
Where is she?

48:54.097 --> 48:55.182
Go to hell.

48:56.475 --> 48:57.351
Okay, then.

50:24.396 --> 50:25.313
Kali.

50:25.981 --> 50:28.524
No, no, no!

50:28.525 --> 50:29.859
Kali. Kali.

50:29.860 --> 50:33.030
- Get bandages please.
- Keep pressure on the wound.

50:33.864 --> 50:35.364
Kali, look at me. Look at me.

50:35.365 --> 50:38.452
Hang in there, okay?
I'm here. It's gonna be okay.

50:39.536 --> 50:42.204
I'm not going to make it.

50:42.205 --> 50:46.834
No, don't say that. You will. You will.
You will make it, okay?

50:46.835 --> 50:48.170
Don't cry, Jane.

50:50.672 --> 50:51.673
My story...

50:52.632 --> 50:54.843
was always going to end here.

50:55.761 --> 50:56.762
No.

50:57.971 --> 50:59.306
No, no.

51:37.302 --> 51:38.220
Holly.

51:41.723 --> 51:42.724
Holly?

52:02.661 --> 52:04.371
How did you find me?

52:05.330 --> 52:06.581
Please.

52:07.332 --> 52:10.293
Please, mister. Don't shoot.

52:11.044 --> 52:12.129
Who are you?

52:12.838 --> 52:16.632
Henry. Henry Creel. I live near here.

52:16.633 --> 52:18.008
Who sent you?

52:18.009 --> 52:21.262
Nobody sent me.
I was in the caves. I heard a scream.

52:21.263 --> 52:24.348
They sent you. They sent you!

52:24.349 --> 52:26.935
You're just confused. You need a doctor.

52:32.232 --> 52:33.400
What's happening?

52:34.985 --> 52:37.069
He's in a memory now.

52:37.070 --> 52:39.029
And he's scared.

52:39.030 --> 52:41.032
He's so scared.

52:51.418 --> 52:54.170
Oh my God. Thank God. Thank God.
Thank God. Thank God.

52:54.171 --> 52:58.549
I thought you two were goners
for a minute there.

52:58.550 --> 52:59.925
Oh, what?

52:59.926 --> 53:02.803
No hug from the big man, huh?

53:02.804 --> 53:05.431
How about a "thank you
for destroying the Huey, Murray."

53:05.432 --> 53:08.602
"That was very brave and... and..."

53:10.187 --> 53:11.271
What's wrong?

53:12.105 --> 53:13.272
Wait.

53:13.273 --> 53:15.442
Kali. Where's... Where's Kali?

53:18.236 --> 53:19.404
Oh God.

53:20.363 --> 53:21.364
El, I'm...

53:22.991 --> 53:24.117
I'm so sorry.

53:42.302 --> 53:43.720
I can jump.

53:45.347 --> 53:47.515
I can jump those boulders to the Abyss.

53:48.016 --> 53:51.144
I'll be right there,
right at the tree. Shortcut.

53:52.312 --> 53:53.771
Henry's still up there.

53:53.772 --> 53:55.606
- If you fall...
- I won't.

53:55.607 --> 53:57.108
If you make it...

54:00.528 --> 54:01.946
I kill him.

54:01.947 --> 54:03.281
Oh, yeah?

54:03.907 --> 54:04.950
And then what?

54:14.751 --> 54:18.129
When I was a kid,
and you found me in the woods...

54:23.593 --> 54:24.803
<i>I was scared.</i>

54:26.388 --> 54:27.389
Really scared.

54:30.934 --> 54:32.727
I didn't understand the world.

54:33.687 --> 54:36.690
I didn't understand... people.

54:40.902 --> 54:42.279
You took me in.

54:47.242 --> 54:48.285
Raised me.

54:48.994 --> 54:49.995
Protected me.

54:50.537 --> 54:51.538
Mm.

55:06.761 --> 55:08.430
You became my dad.

55:17.188 --> 55:20.191
But I'm not... a kid anymore.

55:33.371 --> 55:34.748
And I'm not Sara.

55:45.091 --> 55:47.093
She didn't have a choice to make.

55:52.390 --> 55:53.391
But I do.

55:56.478 --> 55:57.645
And I need you

55:58.313 --> 56:00.607
to trust me to make the right choice.

56:08.073 --> 56:10.992
I need you to believe in me.

57:48.715 --> 57:54.596
<i>Find me.</i>

58:02.812 --> 58:05.272
Ah!

58:05.273 --> 58:10.403
You must resist it.

58:11.279 --> 58:14.573
It will consume you.

58:14.574 --> 58:19.621
It will consume all.

58:49.067 --> 58:50.443
It wasn't you.

58:52.153 --> 58:53.863
<i>It was never you.</i>

58:56.366 --> 58:57.908
Leave me alone.

58:57.909 --> 59:01.411
That's why the Mind Flayer didn't want you
in the cave.

59:01.412 --> 59:02.914
It didn't want you to remember.

59:06.626 --> 59:08.252
I said leave me alone.

59:08.253 --> 59:12.048
You were just a kid, a kid like me.

59:12.882 --> 59:14.509
<i>And it used you.</i>

59:15.176 --> 59:17.595
<i>It used you to bring it here.</i>

59:18.346 --> 59:20.223
You're just like me, Henry.

59:21.140 --> 59:22.392
A vessel.

59:23.476 --> 59:26.687
<i>But you can resist it. Help us fight it.</i>

59:26.688 --> 59:30.525
Don't let it win, Henry, please.
Don't let it win.

59:35.989 --> 59:36.948
No.

59:39.367 --> 59:40.994
It showed me the truth.

59:45.999 --> 59:50.127
It showed me that this world is broken.

59:50.128 --> 59:52.504
That man is broken.

59:52.505 --> 59:56.259
Don't listen to it, Henry.
It is controlling you right now.

01:00:05.101 --> 01:00:08.062
It has never controlled me.

01:00:09.272 --> 01:00:11.357
And I never controlled it.

01:00:22.702 --> 01:00:25.538
Don't you see, William?

01:00:26.247 --> 01:00:28.958
<i>I could have resisted it.</i>

01:00:29.876 --> 01:00:31.919
But I chose

01:00:32.879 --> 01:00:33.963
to join it.

01:00:40.261 --> 01:00:41.304
Oh my God.

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:55.777
It needs... me.

01:01:01.658 --> 01:01:03.284
And I need it.

01:01:10.833 --> 01:01:11.793
We...

01:01:15.463 --> 01:01:16.506
...are...

01:01:18.925 --> 01:01:19.801
one.

01:01:24.639 --> 01:01:25.640
Run!

01:01:26.224 --> 01:01:27.433
Run! Run! Run!

01:01:41.531 --> 01:01:42.782
Dustin!

01:01:47.537 --> 01:01:50.164
- Come on! Come on!
- Let's go!

01:01:52.625 --> 01:01:53.710
Come on!

01:01:55.336 --> 01:01:56.170
Shit!

01:02:08.975 --> 01:02:10.726
Come on, go! Go, go, go!

01:02:10.727 --> 01:02:12.228
Run! Run! Run!

01:03:12.747 --> 01:03:14.122
- She's hurting it.
- How?

01:03:14.123 --> 01:03:15.040
She's fighting Vecna.

01:03:15.041 --> 01:03:16.250
Hive mind.

01:03:26.427 --> 01:03:27.887
So...

01:03:28.638 --> 01:03:32.433
you truly do want to die.

01:03:39.857 --> 01:03:41.608
- We have to help her.
- How?

01:03:41.609 --> 01:03:45.153
The hive mind works in both ways.
If we hurt the Mind Flayer, we hurt Vecna.

01:03:45.154 --> 01:03:47.113
What, hurt Godzilla over there?

01:03:47.114 --> 01:03:50.242
The only way to damage anything
of that scale, we spread out.

01:03:50.243 --> 01:03:52.744
Flank it on all sides.
Just chip away at its hit points.

01:03:52.745 --> 01:03:54.663
"Hit points"? What are you talking about?

01:03:54.664 --> 01:03:55.789
There.

01:03:55.790 --> 01:03:59.836
One of us draws it to that canyon.
The rest take positions on those cliffs.

01:04:00.962 --> 01:04:02.129
Ambush it from above.

01:04:03.381 --> 01:04:05.091
There's just one question.

01:04:06.342 --> 01:04:07.760
Which one of us is bait?

01:04:10.346 --> 01:04:11.681
I am.

01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:36.163
Go!

01:04:38.124 --> 01:04:39.125
Come on.

01:04:57.894 --> 01:04:58.895
No!

01:04:59.478 --> 01:05:00.395
No, no!

01:05:00.396 --> 01:05:02.857
There's nothing we can do!
Come on, please!

01:06:08.714 --> 01:06:11.258
Boom!

01:06:42.748 --> 01:06:44.333
Look out! Look out!

01:06:48.963 --> 01:06:51.674
- This is for Eddie, you son of a bitch!
- For Eddie!

01:07:32.757 --> 01:07:34.800
I'm not afraid anymore.

01:07:42.099 --> 01:07:43.059
We're not...

01:07:44.935 --> 01:07:45.978
afraid...

01:07:49.065 --> 01:07:50.149
of you.

01:08:05.081 --> 01:08:06.165
Yeah!

01:08:07.500 --> 01:08:08.625
We gotta go!

01:08:08.626 --> 01:08:10.086
Run! Shit, shit, shit!

01:08:48.874 --> 01:08:49.875
El!

01:08:53.546 --> 01:08:54.672
Is everyone okay?

01:08:56.590 --> 01:08:57.466
Holly.

01:09:21.490 --> 01:09:22.991
Holly? Can you hear me?

01:09:22.992 --> 01:09:27.037
Holly? Holly, come on. Come on.

01:09:40.801 --> 01:09:41.635
Nancy?

01:09:43.596 --> 01:09:46.472
Yeah. Yeah, it's me. I'm here.

01:09:46.473 --> 01:09:50.477
Yeah, it's me. I'm here. I'm here.

01:09:52.771 --> 01:09:54.148
Holly?

01:09:56.025 --> 01:09:56.901
Hey!

01:09:58.444 --> 01:09:59.445
Hey.

01:10:26.430 --> 01:10:29.767
Okay, get it all out.
You got this. You're gonna be okay.

01:10:30.392 --> 01:10:31.935
Where... Where am I?

01:10:31.936 --> 01:10:35.439
You're safe. You're safe, bud, okay?
We're here to get you home.

01:10:36.065 --> 01:10:37.358
Yeah. Whoa!

01:10:38.067 --> 01:10:41.237
I got you, bud. I got you.
I got you, bud. It's okay.

01:11:44.258 --> 01:11:46.676
Please, please. Come back to me!

01:11:46.677 --> 01:11:49.305
No!

01:11:59.273 --> 01:12:01.108
You fucked with the wrong family.

01:12:10.117 --> 01:12:11.994
Mom, you're killing him!

01:12:12.828 --> 01:12:14.246
<i>Help!</i>

01:12:16.999 --> 01:12:18.959
<i>Why don't you go ahead and go home?</i>

01:12:21.170 --> 01:12:23.129
<i>I didn't run away this time.</i>

01:12:23.130 --> 01:12:24.839
<i>Eddie!</i>

01:12:24.840 --> 01:12:25.966
<i>I love you, man.</i>

01:12:26.550 --> 01:12:27.885
<i>Goodbye, Mike.</i>

01:12:28.552 --> 01:12:30.929
El! El, where are you?

01:12:32.264 --> 01:12:34.849
<i>He did not make me into this.</i>

01:12:34.850 --> 01:12:36.101
<i>You did.</i>

01:12:38.937 --> 01:12:40.272
<i>Will, wake up!</i>

01:12:41.273 --> 01:12:42.524
Go away!

01:12:44.401 --> 01:12:46.236
I just want this to be over.

01:13:38.705 --> 01:13:41.457
- <i>Chief, you copy? Chief?</i>
- Yeah, yeah, I copy. What's going on?

01:13:41.458 --> 01:13:44.001
Well, the noseless bastard's toast.

01:13:44.002 --> 01:13:48.006
We're back in the Upside Down,
and we have the kids.

01:13:51.218 --> 01:13:53.429
How is everybody? Is everybody okay?

01:13:54.138 --> 01:13:56.723
Yeah, the party took a hell of a beating,
but we're okay.

01:13:58.225 --> 01:13:59.268
What about El?

01:14:00.936 --> 01:14:02.146
The whole party.

01:14:07.985 --> 01:14:10.153
<i>So what do we say
you hit the music, old man?</i>

01:14:10.154 --> 01:14:12.489
<i>Destroy the Upside Down once and for all.</i>

01:14:13.198 --> 01:14:14.950
Let's ditch this hellscape.

01:14:16.243 --> 01:14:17.369
Yeah, copy that.

01:14:34.761 --> 01:14:37.723
All right. The countdown begins.

01:14:51.195 --> 01:14:53.655
Hey, stop!
You're gonna get it all over me!

01:14:55.908 --> 01:14:58.035
Hey, hey, I'm nasty too.

01:14:58.619 --> 01:15:00.162
It does stink.

01:15:04.500 --> 01:15:08.169
<i>How can you just leave me standing</i>

01:15:08.170 --> 01:15:11.088
<i>Alone in a world that's so cold?</i>

01:15:11.089 --> 01:15:12.173
<i>The world is so cold</i>

01:15:12.174 --> 01:15:14.426
<i>Maybe I'm just too demanding</i>

01:15:16.011 --> 01:15:19.430
<i>Maybe I'm just like my father
Too bold</i>

01:15:19.431 --> 01:15:22.809
<i>Maybe you're just like my mother</i>

01:15:23.602 --> 01:15:26.271
<i>She's never satisfied</i>

01:15:26.897 --> 01:15:30.275
<i>Why do we scream at each other?</i>

01:15:31.485 --> 01:15:34.278
What are you doing? You're gonna let
more of that crap in here.

01:15:34.279 --> 01:15:37.114
It's either that or pass out.

01:15:37.115 --> 01:15:39.159
Because you smell like...

01:15:40.619 --> 01:15:43.705
I actually don't know what you smell like,
but it's bad.

01:15:55.342 --> 01:15:56.885
Assholes.

01:15:57.761 --> 01:15:59.096
Eh?

01:16:00.013 --> 01:16:01.306
That's good.

01:16:02.891 --> 01:16:04.851
There she is, home sweet home.

01:16:06.144 --> 01:16:09.106
So, Jimbo, I just gotta ask.
How does it feel?

01:16:09.648 --> 01:16:12.400
Feels like I need a nap and a smoke.

01:16:12.401 --> 01:16:14.068
- I thought you quit.
- Yeah.

01:16:14.069 --> 01:16:16.446
That's why it's gonna taste so good.

01:16:26.915 --> 01:16:28.000
Watch out!

01:16:33.964 --> 01:16:35.132
Everyone okay?

01:16:41.138 --> 01:16:43.347
Everyone put your hands up!

01:16:43.348 --> 01:16:44.765
I said, hands up!

01:16:44.766 --> 01:16:46.267
- Move!
- Hey! Get off me!

01:16:46.268 --> 01:16:48.562
Get down! Get down! Get your hands up!

01:16:49.563 --> 01:16:51.314
- I said hands up!
- Oh, wow!

01:16:51.315 --> 01:16:53.775
Okay, okay.

01:16:55.068 --> 01:16:57.820
No! No! That's my sister! Let go of me!

01:16:57.821 --> 01:16:59.531
- Yeah, yeah!
- Okay, okay!

01:17:06.204 --> 01:17:07.538
Let's go! Move!

01:17:07.539 --> 01:17:09.666
- Dustin!
- Holly, what's happening?

01:17:10.250 --> 01:17:13.170
Everybody up! Everybody up!

01:17:14.171 --> 01:17:15.756
El? Do you see El?

01:17:16.465 --> 01:17:19.508
Sergeant! Where's the girl?

01:17:19.509 --> 01:17:21.928
She was right here one second ago.

01:17:25.766 --> 01:17:26.850
She must have escaped.

01:17:35.776 --> 01:17:36.610
Oh God.

01:17:40.614 --> 01:17:43.325
- Mike...
- Get off me! Get off me!

01:17:54.378 --> 01:17:55.294
You...

01:17:55.295 --> 01:17:57.963
You have to get out of there!
You have to get out!

01:17:57.964 --> 01:18:00.466
None of this will ever end,
not if I'm still here.

01:18:00.467 --> 01:18:04.053
No, no. We'll figure something out.
We'll fight back. We always do.

01:18:04.054 --> 01:18:06.055
I need you to talk to the others.

01:18:06.056 --> 01:18:09.475
- No. No.
- I need you to thank them for me.

01:18:09.476 --> 01:18:11.186
For being so kind to me.

01:18:12.020 --> 01:18:14.230
And teaching me what it means
to be a friend.

01:18:14.231 --> 01:18:16.107
No! Please don't do this.

01:18:16.108 --> 01:18:19.944
Mike, I need you
to help them understand my choice.

01:18:19.945 --> 01:18:21.612
But I don't. I don't understand.

01:18:21.613 --> 01:18:22.698
I know.

01:18:23.865 --> 01:18:24.991
But you will.

01:18:25.701 --> 01:18:26.868
One day, you will.

01:18:28.328 --> 01:18:29.830
You understand me.

01:18:32.457 --> 01:18:33.834
Better than anyone.

01:18:34.543 --> 01:18:36.169
You always have.

01:18:37.421 --> 01:18:38.922
From the day we met...

01:18:47.055 --> 01:18:48.390
...you've seen me.

01:18:48.974 --> 01:18:52.143
Well, my name's Mike. Short for Michael.

01:18:52.144 --> 01:18:54.980
Maybe we can call you El.
Short for Eleven.

01:18:59.359 --> 01:19:00.693
The real me.

01:19:00.694 --> 01:19:04.239
<i>I never meant to cause you any sorrow</i>

01:19:09.202 --> 01:19:11.997
<i>I never meant to cause you any pain</i>

01:19:17.377 --> 01:19:20.380
<i>I only wanted one time
To see you laughing</i>

01:19:21.423 --> 01:19:22.549
I love you.

01:19:23.884 --> 01:19:26.510
I love you for exactly who you are.

01:19:26.511 --> 01:19:30.474
<i>I only wanted to see you laughing
In the purple rain</i>

01:19:33.477 --> 01:19:35.479
Please don't leave me, El.

01:19:37.481 --> 01:19:39.399
Please don't do this.

01:19:41.026 --> 01:19:43.028
I will always be with you.

01:19:45.405 --> 01:19:46.698
I love you.

01:19:49.701 --> 01:19:53.747
<i>Purple rain, purple rain</i>

01:19:59.461 --> 01:20:00.419
Goodbye, Mike.

01:20:00.420 --> 01:20:02.671
<i>Purple rain</i>

01:20:02.672 --> 01:20:06.842
El! El! El! El! El!

01:20:06.843 --> 01:20:08.302
- El!
- Mike!

01:20:08.303 --> 01:20:09.763
- Hey, don't touch her!
- Mike!

01:20:13.475 --> 01:20:15.601
Get off me! Get off me!

01:20:15.602 --> 01:20:18.730
El! El! El!

01:20:20.065 --> 01:20:21.608
El!

01:20:27.697 --> 01:20:29.657
El, no!

01:20:29.658 --> 01:20:32.243
Eleven!

01:20:32.244 --> 01:20:34.788
El!

01:20:35.413 --> 01:20:39.501
El! El!

01:21:37.976 --> 01:21:41.479
No!

01:21:47.652 --> 01:21:50.155
El!

01:21:55.243 --> 01:21:58.580
El! El!

01:23:52.527 --> 01:23:54.320
- Check it out?
- Yeah.

01:24:03.079 --> 01:24:06.124
<i>Hi there, strangers. It's been a while.</i>

01:24:06.916 --> 01:24:08.668
<i>I wonder... I mean...</i>

01:24:09.169 --> 01:24:12.047
<i>Do you guys... even remember me?</i>

01:24:13.173 --> 01:24:15.674
Okay, maybe I'm being too modest.
I mean, let's be honest,

01:24:15.675 --> 01:24:19.637
who could forget this soothing voice
with a trace of a Debra Winger rasp?

01:24:20.263 --> 01:24:26.810
That's right. It's me,
Robin Buckley, aka Rockin' Robin.

01:24:26.811 --> 01:24:29.480
Jimmy "Fast Hands" was kind enough
to let me back into the booth

01:24:29.481 --> 01:24:31.065
for a guest stint,

01:24:31.066 --> 01:24:35.612
but you're gonna have to cut me some slack
because I am feeling rusty.

01:24:36.321 --> 01:24:38.572
I mean, what do I even talk about?
You know?

01:24:38.573 --> 01:24:43.745
My go-to subjects are as out of date
as, well, as my friend's bowl cut.

01:24:44.496 --> 01:24:47.082
<i>I mean, there's no soldiers,</i>

01:24:47.957 --> 01:24:49.250
<i>no fences,</i>

01:24:49.918 --> 01:24:52.002
<i>no Big Brother cameras,</i>

01:24:52.003 --> 01:24:55.465
<i>and the only Big Mac I can find
is a Smush Double Patty at Mickey D's.</i>

01:24:56.216 --> 01:25:01.053
<i>People are happy and smiling
and going to the movies.</i>

01:25:01.054 --> 01:25:04.181
But hey, who doesn't wanna see
Indy's new adventure?

01:25:04.182 --> 01:25:06.351
Shit. Uh...

01:25:07.727 --> 01:25:08.895
There we go.

01:25:10.355 --> 01:25:12.564
Sorry about that.
My partner in crime ditched me.

01:25:12.565 --> 01:25:15.735
But, well, as far as excuses go,

01:25:16.694 --> 01:25:18.070
he had a pretty good one.

01:25:18.071 --> 01:25:20.781
Let's go, boys!
Baseball ready! Baseball ready!

01:25:20.782 --> 01:25:23.117
- <i>Now...
-</i> No mental mistakes!

01:25:23.118 --> 01:25:26.161
...<i>I am almost
too superstitious to say this,</i>

01:25:26.162 --> 01:25:27.955
<i>and I'm knocking on some wood here,</i>

01:25:27.956 --> 01:25:33.043
<i>but I think the Hawkins curse
has finally lifted.</i>

01:25:33.044 --> 01:25:35.254
All right, Thomas.
Let's go. Here we go, man!

01:25:35.255 --> 01:25:37.048
<i>- But at the same time...</i>
- Let's go.

01:25:37.632 --> 01:25:40.343
...this isn't even the Hawkins
that I remember.

01:25:41.553 --> 01:25:43.263
It feels so different.

01:25:44.973 --> 01:25:46.641
But maybe it's not the town.

01:25:47.350 --> 01:25:49.769
Maybe it's me that's changed.

01:25:51.187 --> 01:25:52.689
We probably all have.

01:25:54.482 --> 01:25:57.986
At least, that's certainly true
of my friends.

01:25:58.528 --> 01:26:02.782
Who, by the way, are graduating today.

01:26:06.786 --> 01:26:10.956
That's right, Hawkins High class of '89
is walking the podium today.

01:26:10.957 --> 01:26:13.542
I hope you all come out and support them.
I know I will.

01:26:13.543 --> 01:26:16.378
Because if anyone deserves a standing O,
they do.

01:26:16.379 --> 01:26:20.675
So to get their party started,
a new favorite.

01:26:33.062 --> 01:26:35.982
You break any more bones,
you're on your own.

01:26:36.566 --> 01:26:39.109
Because I am done with hospitals.

01:26:39.110 --> 01:26:40.903
Maybe I should be on my own.

01:26:40.904 --> 01:26:41.988
I mean...

01:26:42.572 --> 01:26:43.989
what is going on here?

01:26:43.990 --> 01:26:46.200
What? We're graduating today.

01:26:46.201 --> 01:26:49.537
In two hours.
I think you're getting ahead of yourself.

01:26:50.622 --> 01:26:51.664
Hmm.

01:26:53.124 --> 01:26:55.919
Okay, now you're definitely
getting ahead of yourself.

01:26:56.502 --> 01:26:59.797
I'm sorry. You're just looking,
uh, super sexy right now.

01:27:00.465 --> 01:27:02.383
And you're looking super dorky.

01:27:05.220 --> 01:27:07.222
<i>Here comes your man</i>

01:27:08.932 --> 01:27:10.933
<i>Here comes your man</i>

01:27:10.934 --> 01:27:14.604
Ugh, gag me with a spoon.

01:27:16.731 --> 01:27:18.815
<i>Here comes your man</i>

01:27:18.816 --> 01:27:20.442
You gonna take the picture?

01:27:20.443 --> 01:27:22.695
Already? Please?

01:27:23.279 --> 01:27:26.031
Ma, it's okay.

01:27:26.032 --> 01:27:28.492
- I'm only a day's drive away.
- I know.

01:27:28.493 --> 01:27:30.202
I'm gonna come home
every chance that I get.

01:27:30.203 --> 01:27:31.119
Okay.

01:27:31.120 --> 01:27:33.705
I'm gonna call you so much
that you're gonna wanna change numbers.

01:27:33.706 --> 01:27:34.998
- Okay.
- Okay?

01:27:34.999 --> 01:27:36.583
Okay.

01:27:36.584 --> 01:27:38.001
- I love you.
- I love you.

01:27:38.002 --> 01:27:39.628
Do you wanna take more pictures?

01:27:39.629 --> 01:27:40.671
- Yeah.
- Okay.

01:27:40.672 --> 01:27:44.676
Ooh, so handsome. My valedictorian.

01:27:46.177 --> 01:27:47.511
Superman!

01:27:47.512 --> 01:27:49.429
- <i>All right, rolling.
- Happy graduation.</i>

01:27:49.430 --> 01:27:51.139
<i>Happy graduation.</i>

01:27:51.140 --> 01:27:52.516
<i>- That's nice.
- Class of '89.</i>

01:27:52.517 --> 01:27:53.600
Yeah.

01:27:53.601 --> 01:27:55.519
Shit. Hold on. No, no.

01:27:55.520 --> 01:27:57.354
- Oh God. No.
- Let him hang it back up.

01:27:57.355 --> 01:27:59.481
- Leave the bedsheet.
- No, no, no.

01:27:59.482 --> 01:28:01.066
There's too much light.
It needs diffusion.

01:28:01.067 --> 01:28:03.277
- It's not <i>The Godfather.</i>
- I know it's not.

01:28:03.278 --> 01:28:05.822
- Let him hang it up.
- You get one more take.

01:28:08.533 --> 01:28:10.575
It's been all day 'cause of the artist...

01:28:10.576 --> 01:28:13.245
- Hello?
<i>- Joyce. This is Karen. Have you seen Mike?</i>

01:28:13.246 --> 01:28:15.080
No, I haven't seen him.

01:28:15.081 --> 01:28:17.207
<i>We haven't seen him since last night.</i>

01:28:17.208 --> 01:28:20.253
It's Karen. She can't find Mike.

01:28:22.755 --> 01:28:25.466
<i>Here comes your man</i>

01:28:46.362 --> 01:28:49.699
El! El!

01:28:51.034 --> 01:28:52.702
El!

01:28:53.870 --> 01:28:54.829
Hey, kid.

01:28:58.666 --> 01:29:00.251
Thought I might find you here.

01:29:04.172 --> 01:29:05.465
Your mom's freaking out.

01:29:06.674 --> 01:29:08.509
Can't say I blame her. I mean...

01:29:09.385 --> 01:29:11.887
I don't know if you remember,
but we do have a history

01:29:11.888 --> 01:29:14.057
of kids going missing in this town.

01:29:16.851 --> 01:29:18.603
She won't understand.

01:29:19.187 --> 01:29:24.192
She'll never understand why I can't do it,
why I can't walk the stage.

01:29:25.777 --> 01:29:27.070
It'd be like a lie.

01:29:29.155 --> 01:29:31.948
Like I'm okay with moving on.

01:29:31.949 --> 01:29:33.451
And I'm not.

01:29:35.995 --> 01:29:37.288
I'm not okay with it.

01:29:41.209 --> 01:29:42.502
I had this plan.

01:29:43.461 --> 01:29:48.256
That me and El, we were gonna go
someplace far away,

01:29:48.257 --> 01:29:49.926
and... and no one would find us.

01:29:51.219 --> 01:29:54.930
And I said this thing about going
somewhere with three waterfalls.

01:29:54.931 --> 01:29:57.475
I mean, I... I don't even know
if she believed me.

01:29:58.393 --> 01:30:03.773
Who would? Three waterfalls?
I mean, that's so stupid, childish.

01:30:04.524 --> 01:30:07.735
It was a fantasy plan.
I should've had a real one.

01:30:09.821 --> 01:30:10.863
I just didn't...

01:30:12.615 --> 01:30:15.242
I didn't think that she would just...

01:30:15.243 --> 01:30:16.869
Hey, hey. This...

01:30:21.207 --> 01:30:23.000
It's not your... It's not your fault.

01:30:25.336 --> 01:30:27.171
What happened is not your fault.

01:30:29.173 --> 01:30:30.925
El made her choice.

01:30:32.385 --> 01:30:34.470
Now it's time for you to make yours.

01:30:35.513 --> 01:30:38.349
And the way I see it,
you got two roads ahead of you.

01:30:39.183 --> 01:30:40.685
You got one road

01:30:41.644 --> 01:30:43.895
where you keep blaming yourself
for what happened.

01:30:43.896 --> 01:30:47.233
You keep going over it in your head,
what you could've done differently.

01:30:48.025 --> 01:30:53.156
You push people away, and you suffer,
because that's what you think you deserve.

01:30:55.533 --> 01:30:57.410
And then there's another road...

01:31:00.913 --> 01:31:05.710
where you find a way
to accept what happened.

01:31:06.794 --> 01:31:08.921
Find a way to accept her choice.

01:31:10.214 --> 01:31:13.301
Doesn't mean you gotta like it.
Doesn't mean you gotta understand it.

01:31:14.093 --> 01:31:15.678
And never think about it.

01:31:17.930 --> 01:31:19.223
You just accept it.

01:31:20.808 --> 01:31:23.436
And you live the best goddamn life
you can.

01:31:29.484 --> 01:31:31.777
I've been down that first road before.

01:31:34.322 --> 01:31:35.781
And I don't recommend it.

01:31:38.075 --> 01:31:39.494
And as for El...

01:31:40.745 --> 01:31:43.748
I think you know
what she would have wanted for you.

01:32:05.770 --> 01:32:08.063
- I don't know. Me?
- Yeah.

01:32:08.064 --> 01:32:11.567
- Never been.
- Me neither. But I think she'd like it.

01:32:29.794 --> 01:32:31.044
Good afternoon, everyone,

01:32:31.045 --> 01:32:35.132
and welcome to the graduation ceremony
for the class of '89.

01:32:39.804 --> 01:32:41.806
Mom! Mom!

01:32:49.480 --> 01:32:51.023
Mike.

01:32:51.732 --> 01:32:53.776
I'm sorry, Mom. I panicked.

01:32:54.819 --> 01:32:56.362
You don't have to explain.

01:32:57.697 --> 01:32:58.906
God, look at you.

01:33:01.909 --> 01:33:03.286
You're all grown up.

01:33:04.579 --> 01:33:05.997
I'm so proud of you.

01:33:08.040 --> 01:33:10.501
I'm so, so proud.

01:33:17.466 --> 01:33:18.467
I love you, Mom.

01:33:20.803 --> 01:33:22.221
I love you, baby.

01:33:24.807 --> 01:33:27.767
And now it's my great pleasure
to introduce someone

01:33:27.768 --> 01:33:31.271
who has truly excelled
during their time here.

01:33:31.272 --> 01:33:37.320
Ladies and gentlemen, give a warm welcome
for your valedictorian, Dustin Henderson.

01:33:39.363 --> 01:33:40.406
Yeah, buddy!

01:33:41.866 --> 01:33:43.116
Dustin!

01:33:43.117 --> 01:33:44.117
That's my friend!

01:33:44.118 --> 01:33:45.244
Whoo!

01:33:51.584 --> 01:33:54.420
<i>I just wanted a normal childhood.</i>

01:33:55.254 --> 01:33:57.214
But that childhood was stolen from me.

01:33:58.549 --> 01:34:00.426
It was stolen from us.

01:34:01.302 --> 01:34:03.928
And this past year,
if you wanna know the truth,

01:34:03.929 --> 01:34:06.348
I've been pretty pissed off about it.

01:34:06.349 --> 01:34:07.307
Language.

01:34:07.308 --> 01:34:09.351
But then I thought back
to the past six years,

01:34:09.352 --> 01:34:13.856
and I realized that,
even though there was a lot of bad,

01:34:15.024 --> 01:34:16.901
there was so much good too.

01:34:18.778 --> 01:34:21.029
There's this game I like to play.

01:34:21.030 --> 01:34:23.198
It's called Dungeons & Dragons.

01:34:23.199 --> 01:34:24.783
- Yup!
- Jesus Christ.

01:34:24.784 --> 01:34:28.328
And in this game,
there are two types of chaos classes,

01:34:28.329 --> 01:34:30.623
chaotic good and chaotic bad.

01:34:31.582 --> 01:34:36.294
Now, bad chaos brings
anarchy, destruction, war.

01:34:36.295 --> 01:34:40.257
But good chaos can bring innovation,

01:34:41.425 --> 01:34:42.426
change.

01:34:43.010 --> 01:34:44.303
And this school,

01:34:45.513 --> 01:34:47.472
frankly, it needed to change.

01:34:47.473 --> 01:34:53.228
Because we were so divided
into the jocks, the nerds, freaks.

01:34:53.229 --> 01:34:54.772
And in the chaos,

01:34:55.398 --> 01:34:58.359
all those walls broke down,

01:34:58.984 --> 01:35:00.444
and I made new friends.

01:35:01.195 --> 01:35:04.407
I made friends who were never even
supposed to be my friends.

01:35:04.990 --> 01:35:07.201
This wasn't just me.
I saw this happen with so many others.

01:35:08.035 --> 01:35:10.537
When you get to know people
who are different from you,

01:35:10.538 --> 01:35:13.582
you begin to learn more about yourself.

01:35:14.458 --> 01:35:15.292
You change.

01:35:16.877 --> 01:35:18.087
You grow.

01:35:18.587 --> 01:35:21.131
I'm a better person now.

01:35:21.132 --> 01:35:23.634
I'm a better person because of them,

01:35:24.218 --> 01:35:26.053
because of my friends.

01:35:27.012 --> 01:35:30.099
So, I'm not pissed off anymore.

01:35:31.225 --> 01:35:32.643
But I am worried.

01:35:33.394 --> 01:35:34.228
Worried,

01:35:35.271 --> 01:35:37.440
because now that the chaos is over,

01:35:37.982 --> 01:35:40.775
Principal Higgins
and every square like him

01:35:40.776 --> 01:35:43.862
is gonna do their damnedest
to put everything back in order.

01:35:43.863 --> 01:35:45.822
And I don't want order,

01:35:45.823 --> 01:35:48.366
which is why it's hypocritical
that I'm wearing this thing.

01:35:48.367 --> 01:35:52.036
I mean, we look ridiculous.
What is this? We look like Roman senators.

01:35:52.037 --> 01:35:55.749
I mean, it's not who I am.
I don't think it's who any of us are.

01:35:55.750 --> 01:35:58.918
So, honestly, just screw it.

01:35:58.919 --> 01:36:00.879
- Henderson.
- Yes!

01:36:00.880 --> 01:36:03.173
- Screw the school.
- Henderson! Henderson!

01:36:03.174 --> 01:36:04.632
- Screw the system.
- That's enough!

01:36:04.633 --> 01:36:05.800
Screw conformity.

01:36:05.801 --> 01:36:07.302
- Screw everyone and everything...
- Yes!

01:36:07.303 --> 01:36:09.387
...trying to hold you back
and tear us apart,

01:36:09.388 --> 01:36:12.307
because this, this is our year!

01:36:12.308 --> 01:36:13.808
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

01:36:13.809 --> 01:36:15.019
Yeah!

01:36:16.061 --> 01:36:16.895
Whoo!

01:36:16.896 --> 01:36:18.397
Whoo-hoo!

01:36:25.821 --> 01:36:28.532
<i>The bugle sounds, the charge begins</i>

01:36:29.033 --> 01:36:32.035
<i>But on this battlefield, no one wins</i>

01:36:32.036 --> 01:36:34.914
<i>The smell of acrid smoke
And horses' breath</i>

01:36:35.414 --> 01:36:37.708
<i>As I plunge on into certain death</i>

01:36:40.002 --> 01:36:41.462
Whoo-hoo!

01:36:43.255 --> 01:36:44.465
Settle down!

01:36:45.466 --> 01:36:47.259
Back in your seats now!

01:36:48.302 --> 01:36:51.137
Summer school for all of you!

01:36:51.138 --> 01:36:52.765
And detention!

01:37:09.615 --> 01:37:10.698
- Dustin!
- Dustin!

01:37:10.699 --> 01:37:11.826
Dustin!

01:37:13.911 --> 01:37:16.204
You're a madman.
You're an absolute madman.

01:37:16.205 --> 01:37:19.249
- Higgins totally shit his pants.
- What's he gonna do, expel me?

01:37:19.250 --> 01:37:20.876
- You're crazy.
- Hey.

01:37:21.794 --> 01:37:23.461
Hey, Stacey.

01:37:23.462 --> 01:37:26.297
I just wanted to say what you did up there
was pretty badass.

01:37:26.298 --> 01:37:29.885
Oh. Thanks. I was kind of just going
for a bit of a Belushi thing.

01:37:30.845 --> 01:37:32.679
But if he was in like a Hughes film.

01:37:32.680 --> 01:37:34.722
But I don't know. Does that make sense?

01:37:34.723 --> 01:37:35.682
Yeah.

01:37:35.683 --> 01:37:37.267
- That's okay if you...
- No, totally.

01:37:37.268 --> 01:37:39.103
- Yeah?
- Mm-hmm.

01:37:41.063 --> 01:37:42.189
Okay. Cool.

01:37:43.232 --> 01:37:44.941
- Why'd I say that?
- Dude...

01:37:44.942 --> 01:37:48.821
Hey, so I'm having a party later tonight.

01:37:49.363 --> 01:37:50.865
You guys should come.

01:37:51.991 --> 01:37:53.908
- Wait.
- Did that just happen?

01:37:53.909 --> 01:37:55.618
Should we go?

01:37:55.619 --> 01:37:57.705
Is that rhetorical?

01:37:58.205 --> 01:38:00.123
No. Screw that.

01:38:00.124 --> 01:38:01.458
I got a better idea.

01:38:02.001 --> 01:38:03.002
Way better.

01:38:05.963 --> 01:38:08.965
I'm just saying, I think
you guys would really dig New York.

01:38:08.966 --> 01:38:10.592
- Yeah.
- How much is rent?

01:38:10.593 --> 01:38:13.386
- Thinking about moving?
- You wanna come live with me?

01:38:13.387 --> 01:38:15.054
You're serious? Come on.

01:38:15.055 --> 01:38:18.976
I mean, look at this place.
The sunset, the view.

01:38:20.144 --> 01:38:21.353
Whoo!

01:38:21.854 --> 01:38:24.522
You guys are seriously telling me
you don't miss any of this?

01:38:24.523 --> 01:38:25.481
Mm.

01:38:25.482 --> 01:38:26.691
No.

01:38:26.692 --> 01:38:30.820
The forest, the quarry,
Family Video, the Hawk?

01:38:30.821 --> 01:38:32.447
No.

01:38:32.448 --> 01:38:35.366
No, I couldn't come back here
if you paid me a million bucks.

01:38:35.367 --> 01:38:38.536
Mm. You'd need a lot less than a million,
I'll tell you that.

01:38:38.537 --> 01:38:40.623
Prices are still way down.

01:38:42.124 --> 01:38:44.417
There's actually this rad place
over in Forest Hills.

01:38:44.418 --> 01:38:47.629
I can't quite afford it yet,
but I'm close.

01:38:47.630 --> 01:38:49.797
And that is on a coach's salary.

01:38:49.798 --> 01:38:51.883
- Don't forget sex ed teacher.
- That's true.

01:38:51.884 --> 01:38:53.469
They have you teaching sex ed?

01:38:54.053 --> 01:38:56.095
It's part of the gig.

01:38:56.096 --> 01:38:59.307
If I had a question about an STD,
you'd be the first person I'd come to.

01:38:59.308 --> 01:39:00.643
Thank you?

01:39:02.061 --> 01:39:03.102
No, I love it.

01:39:03.103 --> 01:39:05.021
I love teaching these kids, you know?

01:39:05.022 --> 01:39:07.315
I get to teach them
about the miracle of life,

01:39:07.316 --> 01:39:11.945
and how to not start it accidentally.

01:39:11.946 --> 01:39:14.656
And this time,
I'm in control of the grades.

01:39:14.657 --> 01:39:17.408
And why do I feel
like you go pretty easy there?

01:39:17.409 --> 01:39:18.868
I have a strict A policy.

01:39:18.869 --> 01:39:21.579
- Uh-huh.
- B, if you're a real knucklehead.

01:39:21.580 --> 01:39:22.872
That's about as low as I go.

01:39:22.873 --> 01:39:24.750
Hell, can you come and teach at NYU?

01:39:25.876 --> 01:39:28.503
I mean, what, I'm gonna grade your movie

01:39:28.504 --> 01:39:31.547
about capitalism,
cannibalism, or whatever?

01:39:31.548 --> 01:39:33.800
No, it's anti-capitalist. <i>The Consumer.</i>

01:39:33.801 --> 01:39:37.971
It's a metaphor. The more she eats,
the hungrier she gets.

01:39:37.972 --> 01:39:39.347
- Right.
- Okay.

01:39:39.348 --> 01:39:41.349
- Well, I mean, it's a working...
- Obviously.

01:39:41.350 --> 01:39:43.851
- That's the working title.
- It's good.

01:39:43.852 --> 01:39:45.270
Mm-hmm.

01:39:46.397 --> 01:39:49.649
Now, Smith. Smith, I... I would consider.

01:39:49.650 --> 01:39:50.692
Oh, really?

01:39:50.693 --> 01:39:53.194
Is it the lectures on Steinem
that draw you

01:39:53.195 --> 01:39:55.114
or the high concentration of women?

01:39:55.906 --> 01:39:58.033
Can't it be both?

01:39:59.368 --> 01:40:00.868
What about you, Nance?

01:40:00.869 --> 01:40:02.371
How are the babes at Emerson?

01:40:02.955 --> 01:40:03.789
Oh, um...

01:40:04.957 --> 01:40:06.041
I wouldn't know.

01:40:07.960 --> 01:40:09.086
I dropped out.

01:40:09.670 --> 01:40:10.837
No way. What?

01:40:10.838 --> 01:40:14.048
Ho, ho, ho! I knew it.
You became a Navy SEAL.

01:40:14.049 --> 01:40:16.134
Oh no, not quite. I...

01:40:16.135 --> 01:40:18.386
I took a job at the <i>Herald.</i>

01:40:18.387 --> 01:40:22.056
Which... It sounds fancier like that.
It's a trainee position.

01:40:22.057 --> 01:40:24.892
But I don't know.
I was just sick of school

01:40:24.893 --> 01:40:30.858
and thought I'd maybe get out there
and... try the real world.

01:40:32.776 --> 01:40:34.111
Nancy Wheeler.

01:40:35.112 --> 01:40:36.405
Still full of surprises.

01:40:42.161 --> 01:40:43.203
You know,

01:40:44.621 --> 01:40:47.875
there actually is something
that I miss about this place.

01:40:48.876 --> 01:40:50.002
I miss this.

01:40:51.003 --> 01:40:51.920
Just...

01:40:52.504 --> 01:40:53.672
us.

01:40:54.298 --> 01:40:55.215
Hanging out.

01:40:57.801 --> 01:40:58.969
I miss you guys.

01:41:01.638 --> 01:41:03.140
I really like my new friends.

01:41:04.933 --> 01:41:05.934
But it's...

01:41:06.643 --> 01:41:08.103
It's not the same.

01:41:11.398 --> 01:41:13.025
I don't think it ever will be.

01:41:23.702 --> 01:41:25.037
Okay, Jesus.

01:41:26.538 --> 01:41:27.914
You're killing me, man.

01:41:27.915 --> 01:41:29.625
Let's do something about it.

01:41:31.794 --> 01:41:33.212
I don't know. We could...

01:41:34.463 --> 01:41:35.464
meet up.

01:41:36.799 --> 01:41:38.050
Once a month, here.

01:41:38.634 --> 01:41:43.054
Yeah, or... or maybe somewhere
just more neutral.

01:41:43.055 --> 01:41:44.388
- Like...
- Okay.

01:41:44.389 --> 01:41:48.309
What's a city between Hawkins,
and Massachusetts, New York?

01:41:48.310 --> 01:41:49.394
Louisville.

01:41:50.062 --> 01:41:51.312
- Uh, Philly.
- Philly.

01:41:51.313 --> 01:41:54.440
I have an uncle who lives in Philly.
He's weird, but he's got a big house.

01:41:54.441 --> 01:41:56.943
- Does it have a basement?
- Yeah.

01:41:56.944 --> 01:41:58.820
- And a boiler room?
- A boiler room?

01:41:58.821 --> 01:41:59.905
Yeah.

01:42:00.030 --> 01:42:02.824
Oh my God, it's perfect.
You know, for the hideout.

01:42:02.825 --> 01:42:05.953
You know, where she traps all the men
and then burns their bodies.

01:42:06.912 --> 01:42:07.954
<i>- The Consumer.
- The Consumer.</i>

01:42:07.955 --> 01:42:10.873
- What do you think I'm talking about?
- I thought you were trying to kill us.

01:42:10.874 --> 01:42:11.958
Oh no.

01:42:11.959 --> 01:42:17.296
Okay, okay. Yeah, so we'll meet
at Robin's weird uncle's house,

01:42:17.297 --> 01:42:18.965
and we'll drink and reminisce

01:42:18.966 --> 01:42:23.679
and make Jonathan's
anti-capitalist cannibal movie.

01:42:25.139 --> 01:42:27.099
Starting next month.

01:42:29.226 --> 01:42:30.144
Yeah, I'm in.

01:42:32.020 --> 01:42:33.021
I'm in.

01:42:37.484 --> 01:42:39.570
To nothing ever keeping us apart.

01:42:41.113 --> 01:42:43.949
Including overbearing significant others.

01:42:44.950 --> 01:42:46.076
School.

01:42:46.910 --> 01:42:47.828
Mortgages.

01:42:48.704 --> 01:42:49.538
And kids.

01:42:50.706 --> 01:42:52.332
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

01:42:58.422 --> 01:43:00.673
Yeah, Steve. Kids?

01:43:00.674 --> 01:43:03.969
I don't know, guys.
I think Kristen might be the one.

01:43:06.555 --> 01:43:09.557
So, didn't you say the same thing
about Dawn?

01:43:09.558 --> 01:43:10.975
- No.
- And Margaret.

01:43:10.976 --> 01:43:11.934
And Julie.

01:43:11.935 --> 01:43:15.104
I did not say that about Julie.
She was drama from the start.

01:43:15.105 --> 01:43:16.023
Drama?

01:43:16.523 --> 01:43:18.733
Like, is she a good actor?

01:43:18.734 --> 01:43:20.067
Yeah, you do not wanna...

01:43:20.068 --> 01:43:21.235
I mean, I'm looking.

01:43:21.236 --> 01:43:23.906
- No, no, no. Not there.
- Yeah, have her come along.

01:43:47.179 --> 01:43:51.474
Chief. Mrs. Byers. Always a pleasure.

01:43:51.475 --> 01:43:53.059
Are we ready to order?

01:43:53.060 --> 01:43:54.560
Uh, yeah.

01:43:54.561 --> 01:44:00.150
Yeah. We're gonna have a bottle
of the Cabernet Sauv...

01:44:00.943 --> 01:44:03.736
- Sauvignon.
- Yeah. Cabernet Sauvignon.

01:44:03.737 --> 01:44:07.365
And we'll have some caviar to start.

01:44:07.366 --> 01:44:10.743
And we will have
two of the filet specials,

01:44:10.744 --> 01:44:13.038
however the chef would like
to prepare them.

01:44:13.538 --> 01:44:14.997
- Very good, sir.
- Okay.

01:44:14.998 --> 01:44:16.332
- Hop!
- What?

01:44:16.333 --> 01:44:19.628
It's a big day.
It's a once-in-a-lifetime day.

01:44:20.379 --> 01:44:23.631
You raised two beautiful boys
into incredible men.

01:44:23.632 --> 01:44:26.593
They had a lot more to overcome
than just puberty.

01:44:27.386 --> 01:44:28.637
You should be happy.

01:44:30.555 --> 01:44:32.057
You should be proud.

01:44:32.683 --> 01:44:33.976
I am, but...

01:44:34.643 --> 01:44:35.727
It's just...

01:44:36.353 --> 01:44:37.895
It's gonna be quiet in that cabin.

01:44:37.896 --> 01:44:40.022
It's just us and the crickets.

01:44:40.023 --> 01:44:44.527
Ugh, the crickets. Yeah. I don't like
the sound of those crickets anymore.

01:44:44.528 --> 01:44:45.529
Thank you.

01:44:46.280 --> 01:44:47.530
I wish, uh...

01:44:47.531 --> 01:44:49.740
I wish it was the sound
of something different.

01:44:49.741 --> 01:44:52.868
Maybe, um, squawk of seagulls

01:44:52.869 --> 01:44:57.248
or, uh, waves gently lapping on the beach.

01:44:57.249 --> 01:45:00.294
Well, that sounds nice.

01:45:01.295 --> 01:45:02.296
Could be real.

01:45:05.173 --> 01:45:08.050
I'm just saying there's nothing
tying us down here anymore.

01:45:08.051 --> 01:45:12.430
But you seem to think
our bank account is bigger than it is.

01:45:12.431 --> 01:45:13.347
Could be.

01:45:13.348 --> 01:45:15.725
I got a call from my buddy
in the New York days.

01:45:15.726 --> 01:45:17.811
Montauk's looking
for a new chief of police.

01:45:18.603 --> 01:45:21.814
Town's up and coming. It'd be 20% more.

01:45:21.815 --> 01:45:24.066
I know that's not big enough
for a mansion or anything,

01:45:24.067 --> 01:45:26.360
but it's... significant.

01:45:26.361 --> 01:45:29.948
Kids would be closer.
Just a little quick trip into the city.

01:45:30.449 --> 01:45:31.450
You and me?

01:45:32.659 --> 01:45:33.910
We could start again.

01:45:34.453 --> 01:45:35.454
Fresh.

01:45:36.705 --> 01:45:37.621
Together.

01:45:37.622 --> 01:45:39.123
Are you kidding?

01:45:39.124 --> 01:45:40.916
We don't have to figure out
anything tonight.

01:45:40.917 --> 01:45:42.961
We don't have to decide anything, but, um...

01:45:45.505 --> 01:45:46.964
That's not true.

01:45:46.965 --> 01:45:47.924
What...?

01:45:49.760 --> 01:45:52.596
There's one thing
I would like to decide tonight.

01:46:04.983 --> 01:46:05.942
Who's...?

01:46:13.450 --> 01:46:16.952
<i>At last</i>

01:46:16.953 --> 01:46:18.121
Joyce Byers.

01:46:19.331 --> 01:46:22.583
<i>My love has come along</i>

01:46:22.584 --> 01:46:24.753
Will you spend the rest of your life

01:46:25.337 --> 01:46:30.842
with a tired, grumpy, stubborn old man
who loves you very much?

01:46:33.845 --> 01:46:36.640
Yes. I will.

01:46:42.813 --> 01:46:47.484
<i>Oh, well, at last</i>

01:46:50.612 --> 01:46:54.408
<i>The skies above are blue</i>

01:46:57.911 --> 01:47:02.916
<i>My heart was wrapped up in clover</i>

01:47:05.836 --> 01:47:10.632
<i>The night that I looked at you</i>

01:47:11.174 --> 01:47:16.888
<i>At last</i>

01:47:22.978 --> 01:47:26.648
<i>Ooh</i>

01:47:33.697 --> 01:47:36.032
<i>A hushed quiet falls over the town.</i>

01:47:36.992 --> 01:47:40.453
<i>Frightened villagers watch
from rooftops and alleyways, wondering,</i>

01:47:40.454 --> 01:47:42.038
<i>how will this all end?</i>

01:47:43.165 --> 01:47:46.417
The sound of boots echo across the square

01:47:46.418 --> 01:47:49.420
as Strahd von Zarovich strides up
to Dustin the Bard.

01:47:49.421 --> 01:47:51.088
- Don't do this.
- The vampire lord lunges.

01:47:51.089 --> 01:47:52.923
- No!
- Plunging its fangs into his throat.

01:47:52.924 --> 01:47:55.176
Onlookers gasp as his body collapses.

01:47:55.177 --> 01:47:59.346
His lute clatters across the cobblestone,
letting out a final mournful note.

01:47:59.347 --> 01:48:00.389
Son of a bitch!

01:48:00.390 --> 01:48:04.768
A lone hero remains, Will the Wise,
Barovia's last and only hope.

01:48:04.769 --> 01:48:07.438
Cast Meteor Swarm. Take out the bastard.

01:48:07.439 --> 01:48:08.814
- I can't.
- Why not?

01:48:08.815 --> 01:48:11.025
He's in the range
of the suppression stone. No magic.

01:48:11.026 --> 01:48:12.860
Then just whack him with your staff.

01:48:12.861 --> 01:48:15.864
And inflict six points of damage.
He has 30 HP left.

01:48:17.782 --> 01:48:18.949
Okay, so now what?

01:48:18.950 --> 01:48:21.786
- That's it.
- Nothing.

01:48:22.370 --> 01:48:23.622
What do you mean, nothing?

01:48:25.081 --> 01:48:26.624
- Checkmate.
- We lost.

01:48:26.625 --> 01:48:30.962
So after all of that,
Strahd von Douchebag just wins?

01:48:31.963 --> 01:48:34.840
- This game is bullshit!
- I agree.

01:48:34.841 --> 01:48:37.760
Stupid, goddamn waste of time!

01:48:37.761 --> 01:48:40.764
Strahd takes great pleasure in your anger.

01:48:44.643 --> 01:48:47.186
Time to join your friends, sorcerer.

01:48:47.187 --> 01:48:50.397
Just get it over with and roll.
I don't wanna hear his shit anymore.

01:48:50.398 --> 01:48:51.483
All right.

01:48:56.196 --> 01:49:00.450
The mage. From the Abbey of St. Markovia.
She said we can summon her.

01:49:01.493 --> 01:49:02.702
When at our lowest depth.

01:49:03.286 --> 01:49:05.621
The incantation to summon her.
What's the incantation?

01:49:05.622 --> 01:49:08.290
- What is the incantation?
- Will! Will!

01:49:08.291 --> 01:49:12.795
"Oh, mage! Arise and end our fall
from darkened paths and secrets deep."

01:49:12.796 --> 01:49:15.382
"Come forth and help your promise keep."

01:49:17.259 --> 01:49:18.259
Nothing happens.

01:49:18.260 --> 01:49:20.094
- Come on, man.
- Why?

01:49:20.095 --> 01:49:21.971
Then why do we even have the incantation?

01:49:21.972 --> 01:49:23.389
- What?
- Wait.

01:49:23.390 --> 01:49:24.516
Wait, wait.

01:49:25.141 --> 01:49:27.685
A purple light begins to shine
through the mist.

01:49:27.686 --> 01:49:29.854
Growing brighter and brighter.

01:49:31.064 --> 01:49:31.982
It's a portal.

01:49:33.233 --> 01:49:35.151
And out of this portal steps...

01:49:35.777 --> 01:49:37.821
the Mage of St. Markovia!

01:49:42.659 --> 01:49:46.870
The mage holds out her hands, and shoom,
a beam of powerful light shoots forward.

01:49:46.871 --> 01:49:48.914
Strahd lets out a piercing...

01:49:48.915 --> 01:49:52.669
...as his body shrivels, burns,
and turns to ash.

01:49:54.045 --> 01:49:55.922
Bada-boom!

01:49:56.506 --> 01:49:58.883
How do you like that?

01:49:59.801 --> 01:50:01.469
Whoo!

01:50:02.178 --> 01:50:05.139
The misty gloom that shrouds the village
of Barovia evaporates,

01:50:05.140 --> 01:50:07.433
and you are met
with cheers from the townsfolk.

01:50:07.434 --> 01:50:10.269
In honor of your courage and bravery,
they give you medals,

01:50:10.270 --> 01:50:13.315
and you are all awarded
1,000 pieces of gold each.

01:50:15.317 --> 01:50:16.525
Flush with wealth and honor,

01:50:16.526 --> 01:50:19.695
you live out the rest of your lives
in comfort and in happiness.

01:50:19.696 --> 01:50:21.780
Aaaaah!

01:50:21.781 --> 01:50:23.324
The end.

01:50:23.325 --> 01:50:25.618
- Great campaign.
- Good campaign, buddy.

01:50:25.619 --> 01:50:26.661
Great campaign.

01:50:27.829 --> 01:50:30.122
Wait, wait, wait. Hold on. That's it?

01:50:30.123 --> 01:50:34.043
Comfort and happiness?
Could you be more trite?

01:50:34.044 --> 01:50:36.504
I thought you were some kind
of master storyteller or something.

01:50:37.297 --> 01:50:39.090
Oh.

01:50:44.721 --> 01:50:47.849
Well, it is true,
the comfort and happiness part.

01:50:48.850 --> 01:50:51.353
But happiness can be found in many places.

01:50:52.562 --> 01:50:55.148
The knight and the zoomer,

01:50:55.982 --> 01:50:59.152
they retire from battle,
and they settle down in a small village.

01:51:01.029 --> 01:51:02.656
<i>With each passing day,</i>

01:51:03.531 --> 01:51:05.200
<i>their love grows stronger.</i>

01:51:17.879 --> 01:51:18.880
The bard,

01:51:19.381 --> 01:51:20.714
craving knowledge,

01:51:20.715 --> 01:51:23.467
makes his way
to the Mage's Guild of Enclave,

01:51:23.468 --> 01:51:26.304
<i>where he spends his days
in their vast library.</i>

01:51:27.180 --> 01:51:30.933
<i>- Though deeply devoted to his studies...</i>
- Hey, buddy.

01:51:30.934 --> 01:51:33.353
<i>...he still makes time
for the occasional adventure.</i>

01:51:46.408 --> 01:51:47.658
As for Will the Wise,

01:51:47.659 --> 01:51:52.163
he travels far and long
to the bustling city of Vallaki.

01:51:53.039 --> 01:51:54.791
It's overwhelming at first.

01:51:55.333 --> 01:51:58.628
<i>So very different
from the village where he spent his youth.</i>

01:51:59.754 --> 01:52:02.005
<i>But it isn't long
before he finds his place there.</i>

01:52:02.006 --> 01:52:02.923
Hey!

01:52:02.924 --> 01:52:05.719
<i>And with that, deep happiness</i>

01:52:06.720 --> 01:52:07.971
<i>and acceptance.</i>

01:52:15.061 --> 01:52:18.273
And the storyteller? What about him?

01:52:21.317 --> 01:52:24.612
The storyteller keeps telling stories,

01:52:25.905 --> 01:52:27.615
stories inspired by his friends.

01:52:31.077 --> 01:52:32.703
<i>One day, he hopes</i>

01:52:32.704 --> 01:52:36.583
<i>their tales of grand adventure
will spread far and wide across the land</i>

01:52:37.459 --> 01:52:39.836
<i>so all can know of their great bravery.</i>

01:52:42.130 --> 01:52:45.467
But there is a story
that he can never tell.

01:52:47.427 --> 01:52:48.803
The story of the mage.

01:52:50.638 --> 01:52:52.682
Or at least not the real story.

01:52:54.350 --> 01:52:55.560
The real story?

01:52:59.272 --> 01:53:00.606
When she cast Sunbeam.

01:53:00.607 --> 01:53:01.858
Get off me!

01:53:04.152 --> 01:53:05.111
Goodbye, Mike.

01:53:06.946 --> 01:53:10.073
She expended the last of her energy,
and she vanished.

01:53:10.074 --> 01:53:11.910
El!

01:53:14.329 --> 01:53:16.998
But has anyone asked themselves
how she cast that spell?

01:53:18.833 --> 01:53:20.502
The suppression stone.

01:53:21.085 --> 01:53:22.879
She couldn't have used her magic.

01:53:26.591 --> 01:53:28.635
In the excitement, no one even noticed.

01:53:29.886 --> 01:53:31.930
But you see, the mage is very clever.

01:53:32.430 --> 01:53:34.681
A cleverness only matched by her sister,

01:53:34.682 --> 01:53:37.477
<i>who, upon hearing the pleads
of the paladin,</i>

01:53:38.394 --> 01:53:39.854
<i>had a change of heart.</i>

01:53:40.438 --> 01:53:41.815
Don't cry, Jane.

01:53:42.357 --> 01:53:43.650
My story...

01:53:44.317 --> 01:53:46.402
was always going to end here.

01:53:50.240 --> 01:53:51.783
But yours doesn't have to.

01:53:53.952 --> 01:53:56.621
Together, the sisters devised a plan,

01:53:57.121 --> 01:53:59.915
a plan to protect the mage
from the Order of the Black Hand,

01:53:59.916 --> 01:54:02.209
<i>who remained hell-bent
on stealing her powers.</i>

01:54:02.210 --> 01:54:05.712
So in order to trick them,
she had to make everyone,

01:54:05.713 --> 01:54:09.175
including her friends,
believe that she was dead.

01:54:09.926 --> 01:54:12.637
And so the sister cast a spell
from far away.

01:54:13.638 --> 01:54:15.931
<i>Safe from the power
of the suppression stone.</i>

01:54:15.932 --> 01:54:18.226
El! Do you see El?

01:54:20.603 --> 01:54:22.105
<i>A spell of invisibility.</i>

01:54:32.365 --> 01:54:35.994
<i>Once the mage escaped,
the sister cast one final spell.</i>

01:54:43.877 --> 01:54:46.379
<i>The mage you saw die was not real.</i>

01:54:48.006 --> 01:54:49.424
<i>She was an illusion.</i>

01:54:54.178 --> 01:54:55.429
Where did she go?

01:54:55.430 --> 01:54:56.639
No one knows.

01:54:57.974 --> 01:54:59.017
No one will ever know.

01:55:00.059 --> 01:55:05.899
But I'd... I'd like to imagine that she's
in a beautiful land, somewhere far away.

01:55:31.633 --> 01:55:34.052
<i>She finds a small town to call home.</i>

01:55:35.762 --> 01:55:38.306
<i>Safe from the danger of the Black Hand.</i>

01:55:40.183 --> 01:55:41.391
<i>And it is here,</i>

01:55:41.392 --> 01:55:42.727
at last,

01:55:43.853 --> 01:55:44.979
that she finds peace.

01:55:46.689 --> 01:55:48.650
That she finally finds happiness.

01:55:49.776 --> 01:55:52.070
And this is just a theory, right?

01:55:52.946 --> 01:55:54.280
How do we know it's true?

01:55:55.823 --> 01:55:56.783
We don't.

01:55:59.744 --> 01:56:01.037
Not for sure.

01:56:03.414 --> 01:56:05.500
But I choose to believe that it is.

01:56:07.085 --> 01:56:08.211
I believe.

01:56:10.463 --> 01:56:11.464
I believe.

01:56:13.925 --> 01:56:15.385
I believe.

01:56:16.803 --> 01:56:17.971
I believe.

01:56:19.389 --> 01:56:20.473
I believe.

01:56:25.061 --> 01:56:28.438
Guys! What's going on?
The lasagna's getting cold!

01:56:28.439 --> 01:56:31.734
Yeah, we... we just finished.
We'll be right up.

01:57:54.859 --> 01:57:57.402
- Holly, how do we play this game?
- Jesus, watch out!

01:57:57.403 --> 01:58:00.238
Jeez yourself!
You said you'd be done an hour ago!

01:58:00.239 --> 01:58:01.948
Look, it's our own little castle.

01:58:01.949 --> 01:58:04.951
I'll look in the manual
for like a starter campaign in here.

01:58:04.952 --> 01:58:06.411
Why do you get to be Dungeon Master?

01:58:06.412 --> 01:58:08.371
Because this was my idea,
and this is my house!

01:58:08.372 --> 01:58:10.207
You told me
this was not going to be nerdy!

01:58:10.208 --> 01:58:11.541
- This is super nerdy!
- Put him down!

01:58:11.542 --> 01:58:13.044
- Did you just fart?
- No.

01:58:13.711 --> 01:58:15.253
Something smells. I'm gonna puke.

01:58:15.254 --> 01:58:16.421
It's just old pizza.

01:58:16.422 --> 01:58:18.757
Old pizza doesn't smell like crusty ass!

01:58:18.758 --> 01:58:20.050
Blame it on the girls.

01:58:20.051 --> 01:58:22.969
Excuse me, girls don't fart.
If they do, it smells like roses.

01:58:22.970 --> 01:58:23.970
Listen to Holly!

01:58:23.971 --> 01:58:26.056
- You get these back when you focus!
- I can't see!

01:58:26.057 --> 01:58:28.683
Okay! You can be a halfling! A halfling!

01:58:28.684 --> 01:58:31.103
You want me to walk around like this
and fall over?

01:58:31.104 --> 01:58:33.772
No, you're sitting down and focusing!

01:58:33.773 --> 01:58:35.858
Give me my glasses back!

01:59:08.141 --> 01:59:09.767
<i>I</i>

01:59:11.352 --> 01:59:13.729
<i>I wish you could swim</i>

01:59:16.399 --> 01:59:18.484
<i>Like the dolphins</i>

01:59:20.027 --> 01:59:21.988
<i>Like dolphins can swim</i>

01:59:25.283 --> 01:59:27.325
<i>Though nothing</i>

01:59:27.326 --> 01:59:30.580
<i>Nothing will keep us together</i>

01:59:33.499 --> 01:59:39.672
<i>We can beat them forever and ever</i>

01:59:41.048 --> 01:59:43.926
<i>Oh, we can be heroes</i>

01:59:45.803 --> 01:59:47.680
<i>Just for one day</i>

02:00:08.201 --> 02:00:09.577
<i>I</i>

02:00:11.704 --> 02:00:13.664
<i>I will be king</i>

02:00:16.500 --> 02:00:18.419
<i>And you</i>

02:00:19.837 --> 02:00:22.173
<i>You will be queen</i>

02:00:25.176 --> 02:00:27.053
<i>Though nothing</i>

02:00:28.387 --> 02:00:30.932
<i>Will drive them away</i>

02:00:33.059 --> 02:00:35.186
<i>We can be heroes</i>

02:00:37.647 --> 02:00:39.482
<i>Just for one day</i>

02:00:42.193 --> 02:00:44.487
<i>We can be us</i>

02:00:45.655 --> 02:00:47.823
<i>Just for one day</i>

02:00:51.327 --> 02:00:52.745
<i>I</i>

02:00:54.538 --> 02:00:58.709
<i>- I can remember
- I remember</i>

02:00:59.835 --> 02:01:01.337
<i>Standing</i>

02:01:03.381 --> 02:01:07.176
<i>- By the wall
- By the wall</i>

02:01:08.010 --> 02:01:09.553
<i>And the guns</i>

02:01:12.014 --> 02:01:15.934
<i>- Shot above our heads
- Over our heads</i>

02:01:15.935 --> 02:01:17.770
<i>And we kissed</i>

02:01:19.438 --> 02:01:23.734
<i>- As though nothing could fall
- Nothing could fall</i>

02:01:24.986 --> 02:01:26.821
<i>And the shame</i>

02:01:29.198 --> 02:01:31.450
<i>Was on the other side</i>

02:01:33.411 --> 02:01:35.538
<i>Oh, we can beat them</i>

02:01:36.706 --> 02:01:39.875
<i>Forever and ever</i>

02:01:41.252 --> 02:01:44.547
<i>Then we can be heroes</i>

02:01:45.798 --> 02:01:47.675
<i>Just for one day</i>

02:01:54.348 --> 02:01:56.726
<i>We can be heroes</i>

02:02:02.815 --> 02:02:05.234
<i>We can be heroes</i>

02:02:11.324 --> 02:02:13.951
<i>We can be heroes</i>

02:02:15.536 --> 02:02:17.747
<i>Just for one day</i>
